{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476345862,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_cuihaff8p92dyt8ml5a35ykr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\"),path=require(\"path\");\nconst hubs=[\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/command-metadata.json\",\".skilled/skills/sk-design/command-metadata.json\",\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json\"];\nconst meta=hubs.flatMap(h=>JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(h,\"utf8\")).map(x=>({command:x.command,source:h})));\nconst allow=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\"utf8\")).map(x=>({command:x.command,id:x.id,source:\"allow-list\"}));\nconst g=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json\",\"utf8\"));\nconst generated=new Set(g.entries.map(e=>e.command));\nconst live=[]; \nconst walk=(d)=>{for(const f of fs.readdirSync(d,{withFileTypes:true})){const p=path.join(d,f.name); if(f.isDirectory())walk(p); else if(f.name.endsWith(\".md\")&&path.dirname(p).startsWith(\".skilled/commands\"))live.push(p);}};\nwalk(\".skilled/commands\");\nconst grouped=live.filter(p=>p.split(\"/\").length===4 && !p.includes(\"/assets/\"));\nconsole.log(\"command md files under hubs:\",grouped.length);\nconsole.log(grouped.map(p=>\"/\"+p.split(\"/\").slice(2,4).join(\":\").replace(/\\.md$/,\"\")).sort().join(\", \"));\nconst liveCmds=grouped.map(p=>\"/\"+p.split(\"/\").slice(2,4).join(\":\").replace(/\\.md$/,\"\"));\nconsole.log(\"\\nNOT in generated bridges:\",liveCmds.filter(c=>!generated.has(c)).join(\", \"));\nconsole.log(\"\\nGenerated bridges not a live grouped command:\",[...generated].filter(c=>!liveCmds.includes(c)).join(\", \"));\nconsole.log(\"\\nmetadata entries:\",meta.length,\"allow-list:\",allow.length,\"doctor route entries:\",g.counts.doctorRoutes);\n'","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"command md files under hubs: 44\n/create:agent, /create:benchmark, /create:changelog, /create:command, /create:diff, /create:feature-catalog, /create:goal, /create:manual-testing-playbook, /create:readme, /create:repo-rule, /create:skill, /create:skill-parent, /create:with-human-voice, /deep:ai-council, /deep:research, /deep:review, /design:chart, /design:diagram, /design:extract, /doctor:agents-md, /doctor:ci, /doctor:deep-loop, /doctor:env, /doctor:git, /doctor:helper, /doctor:install, /doctor:mcp, /doctor:overlay, /doctor:runtime-mirrors, /doctor:setup, /doctor:sk-code, /doctor:sk-skill, /doctor:skill-advisor, /doctor:speckit, /doctor:symlink, /doctor:update, /prompt:improve, /speckit:complete, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:implement, /speckit:plan, /speckit:resume, /speckit:save, /speckit:search\n\nNOT in generated bridges: /prompt:improve, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:save, /speckit:search\n\nGenerated bridges not a live grouped command: /memory:save, /prompt, /spec_kit\n\nmetadata entries: 19 allow-list: 8 doctor route entries: 35\n","metadata":{"output":"command md files under hubs: 44\n/create:agent, /create:benchmark, /create:changelog, /create:command, /create:diff, /create:feature-catalog, /create:goal, /create:manual-testing-playbook, /create:readme, /create:repo-rule, /create:skill, /create:skill-parent, /create:with-human-voice, /deep:ai-council, /deep:research, /deep:review, /design:chart, /design:diagram, /design:extract, /doctor:agents-md, /doctor:ci, /doctor:deep-loop, /doctor:env, /doctor:git, /doctor:helper, /doctor:install, /doctor:mcp, /doctor:overlay, /doctor:runtime-mirrors, /doctor:setup, /doctor:sk-code, /doctor:sk-skill, /doctor:skill-advisor, /doctor:speckit, /doctor:symlink, /doctor:update, /prompt:improve, /speckit:complete, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:implement, /speckit:plan, /speckit:resume, /speckit:save, /speckit:search\n\nNOT in generated bridges: /prompt:improve, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:save, /speckit:search\n\nGenerated bridges not a live grouped command: /memory:save, /prompt, /spec_kit\n\nmetadata entries: 19 allow-list: 8 doctor route entries: 35\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\"),path=require(\"path\");\nconst hubs=[\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/command-metadata.json\",\".skilled/skills/sk-design/command-metadata.json\",\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json\"];\nconst meta=hubs.flatMap(h=>JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(h,\"utf8\")).map(x=>({command:x.command,source:h})));\nconst allow=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\"utf8\")).map(x=>({command:x.command,id:x.id,source:\"allow-list\"}));\nconst g=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json\",\"utf8\"));\nconst generated=new Set(g.entries.map(e=>e.command));\nconst live=[]; \nconst walk=(d)=>{for(const f of fs.readdirSync(d,{withFileTypes:true})){const p=path.join(d,f.name); if(f.isDirectory())walk(p); else if(f.name.endsWith(\".md\")&&path.dirname(p).startsWith(\".skilled/commands\"))live.push(p);}};\nwalk(\".skilled/commands\");\nconst grouped=live.filter(p=>p.split(\"/\").length===4 && !p.includes(\"/assets/\"));\nconsole.log(\"command md files under hubs:\",grouped.length);\nconsole.log(grouped.map(p=>\"/\"+p.split(\"/\").slice(2,4).join(\":\").replace(/\\.md$/,\"\")).sort().join(\", \"));\nconst liveCmds=grouped.map(p=>\"/\"+p.split(\"/\").slice(2,4).join(\":\").replace(/\\.md$/,\"\"));\nconsole.log(\"\\nNOT in generated bridges:\",liveCmds.filter(c=>!generated.has(c)).join(\", \"));\nconsole.log(\"\\nGenerated bridges not a live grouped command:\",[...generated].filter(c=>!liveCmds.includes(c)).join(\", \"));\nconsole.log(\"\\nmetadata entries:\",meta.length,\"allow-list:\",allow.length,\"doctor route entries:\",g.counts.doctorRoutes);\n'","time":{"start":1794476345812,"end":1794476345861}},"id":"prt_1cf2001a8001dUlm8R1v1YHl10","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf1fddca001TyzXTDeYhbRNTb"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476346790,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_8ttydokp54yvtl2budyo4kxp","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"memory:save\\|spec_kit\\|/prompt\\|retired\\|deprecated\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json; echo \"---GEN-COUNTS---\"; grep -n \"typescriptActive\\|pythonActive\\|doctorRoutes\\|commandMetadata\\|allowList\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json | head; echo \"---README---\"; sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"32:    \"command\": \"/spec_kit\",\n35:    \"reason\": \"The deprecated generic Spec Kit bridge remains live for one-release compatibility and has no JSON command entry.\"\n39:    \"command\": \"/memory:save\",\n45:    \"id\": \"memory:save\",\n46:    \"command\": \"/memory:save\",\n53:    \"command\": \"/prompt\",\n56:    \"reason\": \"The Python compatibility scorer still recognizes legacy /prompt while JSON declares /prompt:improve.\"\n---GEN-COUNTS---\n5:    \"commandMetadata\": 19,\n6:    \"allowList\": 8,\n7:    \"doctorRoutes\": 35,\n9:    \"typescriptActive\": 40,\n10:    \"pythonActive\": 50\n---README---\n---\ntitle: \"Command bridges\"\ndescription: \"Authored command-bridge inputs, compatibility evidence and the generated projection consumed by advisor scoring surfaces.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"command bridges\"\n  - \"generated command bridge projection\"\n  - \"command bridge compatibility\"\n---\n\n# Command bridges\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`command-bridges/` is the source boundary for command metadata that is not yet represented uniformly by every scoring surface. The deriver combines live skill metadata with the authored compatibility inputs and writes the generated JSON projection.\n\nThe doctor commands are a third source: the deriver reads `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and writes one bridge per doctor route and per standalone doctor command and per MCP sub-route.\n\n---\n\n## 2. CONTENTS\n\n| File | Responsibility | Authority |\n|---|---|---|\n| `allow-list.json` | Records compatibility bridges for live commands without command metadata. | Authored input |\n| `command-bridges.generated.json` | Stores the derived command-bridge projection. | Generated, do not edit |\n| `derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Reads live metadata and authored inputs, validates uniqueness and writes the projection. | Authored deriver |\n| `scoring-compatibility.json` | Holds TypeScript and Python scoring compatibility mappings. | Authored input |\n| `shadow-diff.md` | Records comparison evidence between generated and live bridge authorities. | Authored evidence |\n\n---\n\n## 3. DERIVATION FLOW\n\n```text\nskill command metadata files\nallow-list.json + scoring-compatibility.json\n.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\n                         |\n                         v\n              derive-command-bridges.cjs\n                         |\n                         v\n              command-bridges.generated.json\n```\n\nThe deriver also updates generated projection blocks in the live TypeScript and Python scoring sources. It writes a generated block of runnable doctor command strings into `lib/render.ts`. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n\n---\n\n## 4. DOCTOR BRIDGES\n\nIds are `command-doctor-<command>-<target>` when the doctor command owns more than one route, and `command-doctor-<command>` otherwise. `skillId` and `ownerMode` come from the router's `skill_agent` tag. A router without the tag fails the deriver with a named error.\n\nThe runnable string is the command plus its target when the command owns more than one route. A standalone entry may set `runnable`, as `/doctor:env` does with `/doctor:env list`.\n\nA new route needs a hand-written entry in both the `typescript` and `python` lists in `scoring-compatibility.json`. Each entry carries only `inventoryId`, `order`, `id` (equal to `inventoryId`) and an empty `description`.\n\nThe deriver fills the TypeScript name, keywords, intent signals and domains from the manifest, and the Python slash marker from the runnable string. A route marked `default_target` in `_routes.yaml` also gets the bare command (for example `/doctor:ci`) as a TypeScript keyword and a Python slash marker, so the bare typed command reaches it. A typed `<command> <target>` names that target, so the bare command inside it does not also match the default target. Python matches a doctor bridge only on a typed slash command.\n\nA doctor bridge passes on its own wording (an explicit-author phrase match). When none passes and no `/doctor:` command was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s own ranker, `doctor-helper-match.cjs`, whether the prompt describes a doctor problem. If it does, `command-doctor-helper` passes, and `/doctor:helper` then names the command. With no skill passing, a ranker score of 10 or more is enough, or 6 or more when the prompt names a problem. Beside a passing skill, the prompt must name a wrong state or a health check, such as `is not registered`, `never converges` or `turn off`. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. A prompt that contains one of a bridge's `lead_phrases` also puts that passing bridge first, so `check my environment variables` leads with `/doctor:env`. For other prompts, a passing skill keeps first place and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. A typed command shows its matching runnable string on the top line. A skill-first brief shows `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` on the second line. The Python fallback matches a doctor bridge only on a typed slash command.\n\nEach `mcp_subroutes` entry becomes the bridge `command-doctor-mcp-<sub_action>`, with the runnable string `/doctor:mcp <sub_action>` and its owner from the `skill_agent` tag in `mcp.md`. Every derived doctor bridge is active in both scorers, and `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` proves each one.\n\nCheck every admitted phrase with `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. HUMAN EDIT BOUNDARY\n\nHumans may edit `allow-list.json`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `scoring-compatibility.json` and `shadow-diff.md`. Regenerate `command-bridges.generated.json` after changing an authored input or the deriver. Do not edit the generated JSON directly.\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION\n\nRun the deriver in check mode from the repository root:\n\n```bash\n","metadata":{"output":"32:    \"command\": \"/spec_kit\",\n35:    \"reason\": \"The deprecated generic Spec Kit bridge remains live for one-release compatibility and has no JSON command entry.\"\n39:    \"command\": \"/memory:save\",\n45:    \"id\": \"memory:save\",\n46:    \"command\": \"/memory:save\",\n53:    \"command\": \"/prompt\",\n56:    \"reason\": \"The Python compatibility scorer still recognizes legacy /prompt while JSON declares /prompt:improve.\"\n---GEN-COUNTS---\n5:    \"commandMetadata\": 19,\n6:    \"allowList\": 8,\n7:    \"doctorRoutes\": 35,\n9:    \"typescriptActive\": 40,\n10:    \"pythonActive\": 50\n---README---\n---\ntitle: \"Command bridges\"\ndescription: \"Authored command-bridge inputs, compatibility evidence and the generated projection consumed by advisor scoring surfaces.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"command bridges\"\n  - \"generated command bridge projection\"\n  - \"command bridge compatibility\"\n---\n\n# Command bridges\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`command-bridges/` is the source boundary for command metadata that is not yet represented uniformly by every scoring surface. The deriver combines live skill metadata with the authored compatibility inputs and writes the generated JSON projection.\n\nThe doctor commands are a third source: the deriver reads `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and writes one bridge per doctor route and per standalone doctor command and per MCP sub-route.\n\n---\n\n## 2. CONTENTS\n\n| File | Responsibility | Authority |\n|---|---|---|\n| `allow-list.json` | Records compatibility bridges for live commands without command metadata. | Authored input |\n| `command-bridges.generated.json` | Stores the derived command-bridge projection. | Generated, do not edit |\n| `derive-command-bridges.cjs` | Reads live metadata and authored inputs, validates uniqueness and writes the projection. | Authored deriver |\n| `scoring-compatibility.json` | Holds TypeScript and Python scoring compatibility mappings. | Authored input |\n| `shadow-diff.md` | Records comparison evidence between generated and live bridge authorities. | Authored evidence |\n\n---\n\n## 3. DERIVATION FLOW\n\n```text\nskill command metadata files\nallow-list.json + scoring-compatibility.json\n.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\n                         |\n                         v\n              derive-command-bridges.cjs\n                         |\n                         v\n              command-bridges.generated.json\n```\n\nThe deriver also updates generated projection blocks in the live TypeScript and Python scoring sources. It writes a generated block of runnable doctor command strings into `lib/render.ts`. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n\n---\n\n## 4. DOCTOR BRIDGES\n\nIds are `command-doctor-<command>-<target>` when the doctor command owns more than one route, and `command-doctor-<command>` otherwise. `skillId` and `ownerMode` come from the router's `skill_agent` tag. A router without the tag fails the deriver with a named error.\n\nThe runnable string is the command plus its target when the command owns more than one route. A standalone entry may set `runnable`, as `/doctor:env` does with `/doctor:env list`.\n\nA new route needs a hand-written entry in both the `typescript` and `python` lists in `scoring-compatibility.json`. Each entry carries only `inventoryId`, `order`, `id` (equal to `inventoryId`) and an empty `description`.\n\nThe deriver fills the TypeScript name, keywords, intent signals and domains from the manifest, and the Python slash marker from the runnable string. A route marked `default_target` in `_routes.yaml` also gets the bare command (for example `/doctor:ci`) as a TypeScript keyword and a Python slash marker, so the bare typed command reaches it. A typed `<command> <target>` names that target, so the bare command inside it does not also match the default target. Python matches a doctor bridge only on a typed slash command.\n\nA doctor bridge passes on its own wording (an explicit-author phrase match). When none passes and no `/doctor:` command was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s own ranker, `doctor-helper-match.cjs`, whether the prompt describes a doctor problem. If it does, `command-doctor-helper` passes, and `/doctor:helper` then names the command. With no skill passing, a ranker score of 10 or more is enough, or 6 or more when the prompt names a problem. Beside a passing skill, the prompt must name a wrong state or a health check, such as `is not registered`, `never converges` or `turn off`. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. A prompt that contains one of a bridge's `lead_phrases` also puts that passing bridge first, so `check my environment variables` leads with `/doctor:env`. For other prompts, a passing skill keeps first place and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. A typed command shows its matching runnable string on the top line. A skill-first brief shows `Also: /doctor:<command> <target>` on the second line. The Python fallback matches a doctor bridge only on a typed slash command.\n\nEach `mcp_subroutes` entry becomes the bridge `command-doctor-mcp-<sub_action>`, with the runnable string `/doctor:mcp <sub_action>` and its owner from the `skill_agent` tag in `mcp.md`. Every derived doctor bridge is active in both scorers, and `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` proves each one.\n\nCheck every admitted phrase with `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. HUMAN EDIT BOUNDARY\n\nHumans may edit `allow-list.json`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `scoring-compatibility.json` and `shadow-diff.md`. Regenerate `command-bridges.generated.json` after changing an authored input or the deriver. Do not edit the generated JSON directly.\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION\n\nRun the deriver in check mode from the repository root:\n\n```bash\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"memory:save\\|spec_kit\\|/prompt\\|retired\\|deprecated\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json; echo \"---GEN-COUNTS---\"; grep -n \"typescriptActive\\|pythonActive\\|doctorRoutes\\|commandMetadata\\|allowList\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json | head; echo \"---README---\"; sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md","time":{"start":1794476346752,"end":1794476346788}},"id":"prt_1cf200a05001Jrr0co2mzhOi0d","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701",