{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476466686,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_b932p52scbpi2xgy8fgb4yjn","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"LINEAGE=\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek\"; grep -c '\"type\":\"iteration\"' \"$LINEAGE/deep-research-state.jsonl\"; grep -n \"^- \\[\" \"$LINEAGE/deep-research-strategy.md\" | head -12; ls \"$LINEAGE/steer.md\" 2>&1","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"1\n35:- [x] Which commands have no active bridge, which bridges point at retired names, and what does one drift-proof command inventory need?\n36:- [ ] Why do plain planning and research prompts return no recommendation, how does command intent compete with skill intent in fusion, and what do the no-slash penalty and mutating-command gate cost in recall versus precision?\n37:- [ ] What must the advisor render inside the 80 to 120 token brief for a model to act on a command, given that advisor_recommend has no kind or runnable field?\n38:- [ ] Which commands are safe to start without asking, which need a question first, judged by what they write and what they can undo, and where should that run-or-ask policy live?\n39:- [ ] Can a model start a slash command itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what is the fallback where it cannot?\n40:- [ ] Which mechanism brings a request typed as plain chat onto the command workflow, and what is the evidence that workflows are hand-rolled today?\n41:- [ ] Which commands never load the mode SKILL.md their metadata names, which skills have no command front door, and should a skill recommendation imply its command?\n42:- [ ] Which benchmark and fixture rows are needed for every command group and for chat-style prompts, and which metrics separate a missed command from a wrongly sta