{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476786171,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_hmiawm2jnqa654urdu1pbv2e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"head -40 .skilled/commands/deep/research.md; echo \"---PLAN---\"; head -40 .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md; echo \"---CONFIRM-YAML---\"; sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"---\ndescription: \"Autonomous deep-research loop: iterative investigation with convergence detection. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\nargument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch\n---\n\n# Deep Start Research Loop\n\nThin router for the deep-research loop. This command verifies the runtime agent, resolves setup and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n\n### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n\n- **DO NOT** dispatch any agent from this document.\n- **ALL** agent dispatching is handled by the YAML workflow steps.\n- **MARKDOWN OWNS SETUP**: resolve setup inputs here first, then hand off to YAML.\n- **YAML START CONDITION**: do not load YAML until ALL required inputs are bound:\n  - `research_topic`, `spec_folder`, `execution_mode`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `stop_policy`\n  - `dry_run` is normalized to `true` or `false`; absence means `false`\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, artifact-writing behavior, convergence detection, synthesis, and memory save behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n\nLoad the presentation contract before showing startup questions, dashboards, checkpoint text, success output, failure output, examples, or next-step prompts.\n\n\n> **EXECUTION PROTOCOL -- READ FIRST**\n>\n> This command runs a structured YAML workflow. Do NOT dispatch agents from this document.\n>\n> **YOUR FIRST ACTION (HARD-BLOCK gate — do not skip):**\n> 1. Run the Unified Setup Phase (BLOCKED gate) through the presentation contract and resolve:\n>    - `research_topic`\n>    - `spec_folder`\n>    - `execution_mode`\n>    - `maxIterations`\n>    - `convergenceThreshold`\n>    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n>    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n> 2. Load the corresponding YAML file from `assets/` only after all setup values are resolved:\n---PLAN---\n---\ndescription: \"Planning workflow, 8 steps: spec through plan only. Modes :auto, :confirm, :autopilot; :with-* modifiers.\"\nargument-hint: \"<feature-description> [:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended|--unattended] [:with-context] [:with-phases] [--level=N]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, opencode_goal, opencode_goal_status\n---\n\n# SpecKit Plan\n\nThin router for the SpecKit planning workflow. This command resolves the execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, and artifact-writing behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n\nLoad the presentation contract before showing startup questions, checkpoints, dashboards, success output, failure output, or next-step prompts.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan-presentation.txt` |\n| Workflow (all execution modes) | `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan.yaml` |\n| Shared save-context tail | `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-save-context-tail.yaml` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. MODE ROUTING\n\n1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for `:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`.\n2. Treat `:with-context`, `:with-phases`, `--intake-only`, `--phases`, `--phase-names`, `--phase-folder`, `--spec-folder`, `--level`, `--start-state`, `--repair-mode`, and relationship flags as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\n3. If no mode suffix is present, use the presentation contract's startup prompt to ask for execution mode.\n4. For `:auto`, resolve required setup inputs using the presentation contract's auto-resolution rules before loading YAML.\n5. For `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`, bind execution mode to `autopilot`; do not alias it to `:auto`.\n6. Load the selected workflow asset and execute it step by step.\n\n### Workflow Flag Surface\n\nThe argument hint names the invocation shape; the whole flag surface is here. Every entry below\n---CONFIRM-YAML---\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP RESEARCH: AUTONOMOUS DEEP RESEARCH LOOP (CONFIRM MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP RESEARCH: AUTONOMOUS DEEP RESEARCH LOOP (CONFIRM MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Deep Research Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative deep research with convergence detection and user approval gates\naction: Run deep-research loop with user confirmation at each phase transition\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: interactive\n  approvals: multi_gate\n  tracking: progressive_research_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_principles:\n  core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n  approach: \"Dispatch focused agent, show results, get approval, repeat or stop\"\n  mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Pause for user at each gate.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# USER INPUTS (from setup phase)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nuser_inputs:\n  research_topic: \"[RESEARCH_TOPIC] - Topic to investigate deeply. REQUIRED.\"\n  spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path. REQUIRED.\"\n  max_iterations: \"[MAX_ITERATIONS] - Maximum loop iterations. Default: 10.\"\n  convergence_threshold: \"[CONVERGENCE_THRESHOLD] - Stop threshold. Default: 0.05.\"\n  convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n  stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Convergence stop policy; max-iterations forces the loop to run every iteration. Default: convergence.\"\n  dry_run: \"[DRY_RUN] - Boolean pre-flight flag. Default: false.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DRY-RUN CONTROL\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ndry_run_control:\n  enabled_when: \"dry_run == true\"\n  default: false\n  applies_to: \"confirm workflow\"\n  purpose: \"Run safe setup and read-only inspection, then stop before side effects.\"\n  safe_operations:\n    - \"Resolve setup inputs and artifact roots.\"\n    - \"Read current state, strategy, focus, and convergence signals.\"\n    - \"Render the next prompt to terminal preview without writing prompt files.\"\n  forbidden_operations:\n    - \"Executor dispatch.\"\n    - \"Persistent state, queue, lock, git index, memory, or graph mutation.\"\n    - \"Reducer refresh or generated artifact writes.\"\n    - \"Child-lineage spawn.\"\n  event_policy:\n    event_name: dry_run_halt\n    sink: \"terminal JSONL preview only; never append to {state_paths.state_log}\"\n    required_fields: [type, event, mode, boundary, step, timestamp]\n    optional_fields: [run, sessionId, generation, detail]\n  halt_hook_rule: \"Before executing any command, dispatch, edit, output, template write, append_to_jsonl, append_jsonl, log_event, mcp_tool, write, or git-index mutation tagged with dry_run_boundary, emit dry_run_halt_event and halt.\"\n  boundary_labels:\n    child_spawn: \"child-spawn\"\n    state_mutation: \"state-mutation\"\n    dispatch: \"dispatch\"\n    reducer_refresh: \"reducer-refresh\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# CONTEXT LOADING\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ncontext_loading:\n  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n  purpose: \"Load prior research context for the topic and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n  retrieval:\n    mechanism: \"continuity-ladder-then-ripgrep\"\n    note: \"File reads only. Nothing here needs a running daemon, and every step is reproducible by hand.\"\n    ladder:\n      - \"{spec_folder}/handover.md when present\"\n      - \"the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md\"\n      - \"the packet's canonical spec docs, spec.md and decision-record.md, for what the first two steps leave open\"\n    free_text_recipe: \"rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -- '{research_topic}' specs .skilled\"\n    recipe_contract: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n","metadata":{"output":"---\ndescription: \"Autonomous deep-research loop: iterative investigation with convergence detection. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\nargument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch\n---\n\n# Deep Start Research Loop\n\nThin router for the deep-research loop. This command verifies the runtime agent, resolves setup and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n\n### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n\n- **DO NOT** dispatch any agent from this document.\n- **ALL** agent dispatching is handled by the YAML workflow steps.\n- **MARKDOWN OWNS SETUP**: resolve setup inputs here first, then hand off to YAML.\n- **YAML START CONDITION**: do not load YAML until ALL required inputs are bound:\n  - `research_topic`, `spec_folder`, `execution_mode`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `stop_policy`\n  - `dry_run` is normalized to `true` or `false`; absence means `false`\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, artifact-writing behavior, convergence detection, synthesis, and memory save behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n\nLoad the presentation contract before showing startup questions, dashboards, checkpoint text, success output, failure output, examples, or next-step prompts.\n\n\n> **EXECUTION PROTOCOL -- READ FIRST**\n>\n> This command runs a structured YAML workflow. Do NOT dispatch agents from this document.\n>\n> **YOUR FIRST ACTION (HARD-BLOCK gate — do not skip):**\n> 1. Run the Unified Setup Phase (BLOCKED gate) through the presentation contract and resolve:\n>    - `research_topic`\n>    - `spec_folder`\n>    - `execution_mode`\n>    - `maxIterations`\n>    - `convergenceThreshold`\n>    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n>    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n> 2. Load the corresponding YAML file from `assets/` only after all setup values are resolved:\n---PLAN---\n---\ndescription: \"Planning workflow, 8 steps: spec through plan only. Modes :auto, :confirm, :autopilot; :with-* modifiers.\"\nargument-hint: \"<feature-description> [:auto|:confirm|:autopilot|:unattended|--unattended] [:with-context] [:with-phases] [--level=N]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, opencode_goal, opencode_goal_status\n---\n\n# SpecKit Plan\n\nThin router for the SpecKit planning workflow. This command resolves the execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, and artifact-writing behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n\nLoad the presentation contract before showing startup questions, checkpoints, dashboards, success output, failure output, or next-step prompts.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan-presentation.txt` |\n| Workflow (all execution modes) | `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan.yaml` |\n| Shared save-context tail | `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-save-context-tail.yaml` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. MODE ROUTING\n\n1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for `:auto`, `:confirm`, `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`.\n2. Treat `:with-context`, `:with-phases`, `--intake-only`, `--phases`, `--phase-names`, `--phase-folder`, `--spec-folder`, `--level`, `--start-state`, `--repair-mode`, and relationship flags as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\n3. If no mode suffix is present, use the presentation contract's startup prompt to ask for execution mode.\n4. For `:auto`, resolve required setup inputs using the presentation contract's auto-resolution rules before loading YAML.\n5. For `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, or `--unattended`, bind execution mode to `autopilot`; do not alias it to `:auto`.\n6. Load the selected workflow asset and execute it step by step.\n\n### Workflow Flag Surface\n\nThe argument hint names the invocation shape; the whole flag surface is here. Every entry below\n---CONFIRM-YAML---\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP RESEARCH: AUTONOMOUS DEEP RESEARCH LOOP (CONFIRM MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP RESEARCH: AUTONOMOUS DEEP RESEARCH LOOP (CONFIRM MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Deep Research Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative deep research with convergence detection and user approval gates\naction: Run deep-research loop with user confirmation at each phase transition\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: interactive\n  approvals: multi_gate\n  tracking: progressive_research_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_principles:\n  core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n  approach: \"Dispatch focused agent, show results, get approval, repeat or stop\"\n  mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Pause for user at each gate.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# USER INPUTS (from setup phase)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nuser_inputs:\n  research_topic: \"[RESEARCH_TOPIC] - Topic to investigate deeply. REQUIRED.\"\n  spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path. REQUIRED.\"\n  max_iterations: \"[MAX_ITERATIONS] - Maximum loop iterations. Default: 10.\"\n  convergence_threshold: \"[CONVERGENCE_THRESHOLD] - Stop threshold. Default: 0.05.\"\n  convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n  stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Convergence stop policy; max-iterations forces the loop to run every iteration. Default: convergence.\"\n  dry_run: \"[DRY_RUN] - Boolean pre-flight flag. Default: false.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DRY-RUN CONTROL\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ndry_run_control:\n  enabled_when: \"dry_run == true\"\n  default: false\n  applies_to: \"confirm workflow\"\n  purpose: \"Run safe setup and read-only inspection, then stop before side effects.\"\n  safe_operations:\n    - \"Resolve setup inputs and artifact roots.\"\n    - \"Read current state, strategy, focus, and convergence signals.\"\n    - \"Render the next prompt to terminal preview without writing prompt files.\"\n  forbidden_operations:\n    - \"Executor dispatch.\"\n    - \"Persistent state, queue, lock, git index, memory, or graph mutation.\"\n    - \"Reducer refresh or generated artifact writes.\"\n    - \"Child-lineage spawn.\"\n  event_policy:\n    event_name: dry_run_halt\n    sink: \"terminal JSONL preview only; never append to {state_paths.state_log}\"\n    required_fields: [type, event, mode, boundary, step, timestamp]\n    optional_fields: [run, sessionId, generation, detail]\n  halt_hook_rule: \"Before executing any command, dispatch, edit, output, template write, append_to_jsonl, append_jsonl, log_event, mcp_tool, write, or git-index mutation tagged with dry_run_boundary, emit dry_run_halt_event and halt.\"\n  boundary_labels:\n    child_spawn: \"child-spawn\"\n    state_mutation: \"state-mutation\"\n    dispatch: \"dispatch\"\n    reducer_refresh: \"reducer-refresh\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# CONTEXT LOADING\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ncontext_loading:\n  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n  purpose: \"Load prior research context for the topic and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n  retrieval:\n    mechanism: \"continuity-ladder-then-ripgrep\"\n    note: \"File reads only. Nothing here needs a running daemon, and every step is reproducible by hand.\"\n    ladder:\n      - \"{spec_folder}/handover.md when present\"\n      - \"the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md\"\n      - \"the packet's canonical spec docs, spec.md and decision-record.md, for what the first two steps leave open\"\n    free_text_recipe: \"rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -- '{research_topic}' specs .skilled\"\n    recipe_contract: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"head -40 .skilled/commands/deep/research.md; echo \"---PLAN---\"; head -40 .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md; echo \"---CONFIRM-YAML---\"; sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml","time":{"start":1794476786136,"end":1794476786168}},"id":"prt_1cf26c050001VioVcmQzfN7wLM","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf26a443001LCsNic4AlUhpOh"}}
