{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476864572,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_ty65w414zx0xnxmf1xr56zf4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n --no-heading \"cannot (run|invoke|start).*slash|slash command.*(invoke|start|run)|model.*slash command|slash command.*model|commands are user\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring --glob '*.md' --glob '*.json' | head -40","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:34:The repository ships 45 slash commands that own complete workflows, but the skill advisor tells the model about skills, not commands. Only `/doctor:*` commands reach the model as a runnable line. Every other command arrives as a raw bridge id such as `command-spec-kit`, or not at all, and no rule says whether the model should run a surfaced command or ask first. A user who chats without typing a command therefore gets a hand-rolled approach where a command workflow exists.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:68:5. **Invocation mechanics.** Whether a model can start a slash command itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what the fallback is where it cannot.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/goal.md:37:**Objective:** Establish, with repository evidence from three model lenses, how the skill advisor should surface every slash command with a run-or-ask decision and how a chat-only request reaches the proper command workflow.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:23:How the skill advisor should surface all 45 slash commands (run-it-yourself vs ask-first), and how a plain-chat request reaches the proper command workflow on every runtime. Ten angles: inventory, scoring, output contract, run or ask, invocation mechanics, chat-only users, skill and command linkage, measurement, prior art, failure modes.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:33:- [x] Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:63:- Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:120:### \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one. -- BLOCKED (iteration 5, 1 attempts)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:121:- What was tried: \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:123:- Do NOT retry: \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:294:- \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one. (iteration 5)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/resource-map.md:2:title: \"Resource Map — How should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime? Work through the ten research angles in section 3 of specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md: inventory, scoring, output contract, run or ask, invocation mechanics, chat-only users, skill and command linkage, measurement, prior art, failure modes. Start from the advisor runtime in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor (command-bridges, scorer projection and fusion, render.ts), the commands tree, AGENTS.md gates 2 and 4, and the prior packets 003-doctor-command-surfacing and system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review. Cite path:line for every claim and name evidence that contradicts a recommendation as well as evidence that supports it.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/003-doctor-command-surfacing/002-doctor-command-routing/spec.md:131:| REQ-005 | When a skill and a doctor bridge both pass the threshold, the skill ranks first in the TypeScript scorer, which is what the Python sort key already does. A prompt that names a doctor slash command keeps the doctor bridge first. The rule is scoped to doctor bridges, because corpus gold labels include command ids such as `memory:save`. | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:776-777`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:4467-4475`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/labeled-prompts.jsonl:20` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/003-doctor-command-surfacing/002-doctor-command-routing/spec.md:149:| REQ-018 | Added 2026-10-16, widened by REQ-028. A doctor bridge keeps first place over a passing skill only when the prompt starts with a doctor slash command. A command quoted inside a longer request does not count. Both scorers apply the same rule. | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:676-680`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:884-887` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/research.md:91:- No rule instructs a model to *type* a slash command; the only command sentence in `AGENTS.md` makes `command-spec-kit` win a tie [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:90].\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/003-doctor-command-surfacing/002-doctor-command-routing/plan.md:81:- **`fusion.ts`** gains one ordering rule. A doctor bridge never sorts above a skill that passes the threshold, unless the prompt contains a doctor slash command. The existing sort starts at `fusion.ts:775`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md:84:Angle 5 (invocation mechanics) with angle 6 started: whether a model can start a slash command by itself on each runtime. Evidence to read: `AGENTS.md` Gate 4 and the `cli-*` skill contracts, the hook/brief delivery surface for each runtime, and any existing \"the model dispatched a command\" precedent such as `output: \"SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]\"`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:5:Angle 5 (invocation mechanics): whether a model can start a slash command itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot. Chosen after iteration 4 established the policy that a surface must express; this iteration asks what each runtime's delivery and command surface can carry.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:12:4. Grepped the model-facing rules for any instruction that has the model type a slash command.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:24:5. No model-facing rule anywhere instructs the model to type a slash command. `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 tells the model to use the hook brief and to run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend …`, and its output line is `SKILL ROUTING: …` [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:69]. The deep-research skill states it \"is invoked exclusively through `/deep:research:auto` or `/deep:research:confirm`\" — a statement about user entry, not model entry [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:1].\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:26:6. The repository already has a precedent for the model executing an *entry point it was told about*: the advisor's outage fallback prints the literal `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"<request>\"}' --format json` line, expecting the model to run it [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:590]. The precedent covers shell entry points, not slash commands.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:34:No runtime in this repository gives the model a tool that starts a slash command; commands are user-typed entry points, and Devin cannot even surface them. Two fallbacks remain, and they should be chosen by intent rather than by runtime: (a) **name it and ask** — the brief prints the runnable command and the model asks the user to type it; (b) **load and follow** — the model reads `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` and executes the workflow it names, which works everywhere. (b) is only legitimate when the user already asked for that outcome and the command's run-or-ask policy (iteration 4) says run; otherwise (a) is the correct move. The important design consequence is that the brief must carry the command string for both fallbacks, and that the doctor-only runnable map has no reason to stay doctor-only.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:38:- \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:47:- Ambiguous input: \"start a slash command\" could mean user-typed invocation or model-initiated workflow execution. Selected interpretation: model-initiated workflow execution, since the research question is what a model does when the user did not type a command.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:54:- Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-config.json:2:  \"topic\": \"How should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime? Work through the ten research angles in section 3 of specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md: inventory, scoring, output contract, run or ask, invocation mechanics, chat-only users, skill and command linkage, measurement, prior art, failure modes. Start from the advisor runtime in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor (command-bridges, scorer projection and fusion, render.ts), the commands tree, AGENTS.md gates 2 and 4, and the prior packets 003-doctor-command-surfacing and system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review. Cite path:line for every claim and name evidence that contradicts a recommendation as well as evidence that supports it.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-config.json:83:  \"researchTopic\": \"How should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime?\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md:36:The mechanism that reaches the command workflow on every runtime is **the brief carrying the command plus an `AGENTS.md` sentence that makes the brief actionable**, with the command file as the executable body. Concretely: `advisor_recommend` gains `kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` (iteration 3); the brief renders `use {skill} → {command} ({policy})`; `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 gains one line saying that when the brief names a command whose policy is `run`, the model executes that command's workflow (loading the command doc), and when the policy is `ask`, it offers the command and waits. Nothing in that chain requires the runtime to expand a slash command, which is why it survives Devin and every future runtime.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md:18:- Topic: How should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime? Work through the ten research angles in section 3 of specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md: inventory, scoring, output contract, run or ask, invocation mechanics, chat-only users, skill and command linkage, measurement, prior art, failure modes. Start from the advisor runtime in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor (command-bridges, scorer projection and fusion, render.ts), the commands tree, AGENTS.md gates 2 and 4, and the prior packets 003-doctor-command-surfacing and system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review. Cite path:line for every claim and name evidence that contradicts a recommendation as well as evidence that supports it.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md:58:- [x] Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md:100:- \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one. (iteration 5)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md:24:5. Even a typed slash command ranks the owning *skill* above the bridge: `/deep:research` boosts `[['system-deep-loop', 1.6], ['command-spec-kit', 0.45]]`, `/deep:review` the same, and `/speckit:resume` boosts `[['system-spec-kit', 0.9], ['command-spec-kit', 0.75]]` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:97]. The typed-command path therefore *is* a skill recommendation by construction; the bridge id surfaces only as a lower-weight runner-up, which is what the spec's brief shows as a bare `command-spec-kit` [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:34].\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:66:      \"text\": \"Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:174:      \"text\": \"Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:411:      \"text\": \"Even a typed slash command ranks the owning *skill* above the bridge: `/deep:research` boosts `[['system-deep-loop', 1.6], ['command-spec-kit', 0.45]]`, `/deep:review` the same, and `/speckit:resume` boosts `[['system-spec-kit', 0.9], ['command-spec-kit', 0.75]]` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:97]. The typed-command path therefore *is* a skill recommendation by construction; the bridge id surfaces only as a lower-weight runner-up, which is what the spec's brief shows as a bare `command-spec-kit` [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:34].\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:633:      \"text\": \"There is no `kind` and no runnable-command field anywhere in the public response; the only command-adjacent field is the optional `workflowMode`, which names a hub mode rather than a slash command [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:307]. The internal `AdvisorRecommendation.kind` seen in iteration 2 is dropped at this boundary because it is optional and not in the schema [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:41].\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:793:      \"text\": \"No model-facing rule anywhere instructs the model to type a slash command. `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 tells the model to use the hook brief and to run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend …`, and its output line is `SKILL ROUTING: …` [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:69]. The deep-research skill states it \\\"is invoked exclusively through `/deep:research:auto` or `/deep:research:confirm`\\\" — a statement about user entry, not model entry [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:1].\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:832:      \"text\": \"The repository already has a precedent for the model executing an *entry point it was told about*: the advisor's outage fallback prints the literal `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"<request>\\\"}' --format json` line, expecting the model to run it [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:590]. The precedent covers shell entry points, not slash commands.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:1225:      \"text\": \"Prior art from outside this repository, marked as inference because no external page was fetched in this session: agent harnesses expose slash commands as user-invoked entries, not model-callable tools, and the `AGENTS.md` convention exists precisely so one instruction file can serve several harnesses [INFERENCE: from the per-runtime mirrors above plus the absence of any model-invoked command surface in seven adapters].\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:1469:      \"text\": \"\\\"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\\\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md:17:2. There is no `kind` and no runnable-command field anywhere in the public response; the only command-adjacent field is the optional `workflowMode`, which names a hub mode rather than a slash command [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:307]. The internal `AdvisorRecommendation.kind` seen in iteration 2 is dropped at this boundary because it is optional and not in the schema [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:41].\n","metadata":{"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:34:The repository ships 45 slash commands that own complete workflows, but the skill advisor tells the model about skills, not commands. Only `/doctor:*` commands reach the model as a runnable line. Every other command arrives as a raw bridge id such as `command-spec-kit`, or not at all, and no rule says whether the model should run a surfaced command or ask first. A user who chats without typing a command therefore gets a hand-rolled approach where a command workflow exists.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:68:5. **Invocation mechanics.** Whether a model can start a slash command itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what the fallback is where it cannot.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/goal.md:37:**Objective:** Establish, with repository evidence from three model lenses, how the skill advisor should surface every slash command with a run-or-ask decision and how a chat-only request reaches the proper command workflow.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:23:How the skill advisor should surface all 45 slash commands (run-it-yourself vs ask-first), and how a plain-chat request reaches the proper command workflow on every runtime. Ten angles: inventory, scoring, output contract, run or ask, invocation mechanics, chat-only users, skill and command linkage, measurement, prior art, failure modes.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:33:- [x] Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:63:- Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:120:### \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one. -- BLOCKED (iteration 5, 1 attempts)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:121:- What was tried: \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:123:- Do NOT retry: \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:294:- \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one. (iteration 5)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/resource-map.md:2:title: \"Resource Map — How should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime? Work through the ten research angles in section 3 of specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md: inventory, scoring, output contract, run or ask, invocation mechanics, chat-only users, skill and command linkage, measurement, prior art, failure modes. Start from the advisor runtime in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor (command-bridges, scorer projection and fusion, render.ts), the commands tree, AGENTS.md gates 2 and 4, and the prior packets 003-doctor-command-surfacing and system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review. Cite path:line for every claim and name evidence that contradicts a recommendation as well as evidence that supports it.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/003-doctor-command-surfacing/002-doctor-command-routing/spec.md:131:| REQ-005 | When a skill and a doctor bridge both pass the threshold, the skill ranks first in the TypeScript scorer, which is what the Python sort key already does. A prompt that names a doctor slash command keeps the doctor bridge first. The rule is scoped to doctor bridges, because corpus gold labels include command ids such as `memory:save`. | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:776-777`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:4467-4475`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/labeled-prompts.jsonl:20` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/003-doctor-command-surfacing/002-doctor-command-routing/spec.md:149:| REQ-018 | Added 2026-10-16, widened by REQ-028. A doctor bridge keeps first place over a passing skill only when the prompt starts with a doctor slash command. A command quoted inside a longer request does not count. Both scorers apply the same rule. | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:676-680`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:884-887` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/research.md:91:- No rule instructs a model to *type* a slash command; the only command sentence in `AGENTS.md` makes `command-spec-kit` win a tie [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:90].\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/003-doctor-command-surfacing/002-doctor-command-routing/plan.md:81:- **`fusion.ts`** gains one ordering rule. A doctor bridge never sorts above a skill that passes the threshold, unless the prompt contains a doctor slash command. The existing sort starts at `fusion.ts:775`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md:84:Angle 5 (invocation mechanics) with angle 6 started: whether a model can start a slash command by itself on each runtime. Evidence to read: `AGENTS.md` Gate 4 and the `cli-*` skill contracts, the hook/brief delivery surface for each runtime, and any existing \"the model dispatched a command\" precedent such as `output: \"SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]\"`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:5:Angle 5 (invocation mechanics): whether a model can start a slash command itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot. Chosen after iteration 4 established the policy that a surface must express; this iteration asks what each runtime's delivery and command surface can carry.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:12:4. Grepped the model-facing rules for any instruction that has the model type a slash command.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:24:5. No model-facing rule anywhere instructs the model to type a slash command. `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 tells the model to use the hook brief and to run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend …`, and its output line is `SKILL ROUTING: …` [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:69]. The deep-research skill states it \"is invoked exclusively through `/deep:research:auto` or `/deep:research:confirm`\" — a statement about user entry, not model entry [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:1].\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:26:6. The repository already has a precedent for the model executing an *entry point it was told about*: the advisor's outage fallback prints the literal `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"<request>\"}' --format json` line, expecting the model to run it [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:590]. The precedent covers shell entry points, not slash commands.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:34:No runtime in this repository gives the model a tool that starts a slash command; commands are user-typed entry points, and Devin cannot even surface them. Two fallbacks remain, and they should be chosen by intent rather than by runtime: (a) **name it and ask** — the brief prints the runnable command and the model asks the user to type it; (b) **load and follow** — the model reads `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` and executes the workflow it names, which works everywhere. (b) is only legitimate when the user already asked for that outcome and the command's run-or-ask policy (iteration 4) says run; otherwise (a) is the correct move. The important design consequence is that the brief must carry the command string for both fallbacks, and that the doctor-only runnable map has no reason to stay doctor-only.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:38:- \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:47:- Ambiguous input: \"start a slash command\" could mean user-typed invocation or model-initiated workflow execution. Selected interpretation: model-initiated workflow execution, since the research question is what a model does when the user did not type a command.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md:54:- Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-config.json:2:  \"topic\": \"How should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime? Work through the ten research angles in section 3 of specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md: inventory, scoring, output contract, run or ask, invocation mechanics, chat-only users, skill and command linkage, measurement, prior art, failure modes. Start from the advisor runtime in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor (command-bridges, scorer projection and fusion, render.ts), the commands tree, AGENTS.md gates 2 and 4, and the prior packets 003-doctor-command-surfacing and system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review. Cite path:line for every claim and name evidence that contradicts a recommendation as well as evidence that supports it.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-config.json:83:  \"researchTopic\": \"How should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime?\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md:36:The mechanism that reaches the command workflow on every runtime is **the brief carrying the command plus an `AGENTS.md` sentence that makes the brief actionable**, with the command file as the executable body. Concretely: `advisor_recommend` gains `kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` (iteration 3); the brief renders `use {skill} → {command} ({policy})`; `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 gains one line saying that when the brief names a command whose policy is `run`, the model executes that command's workflow (loading the command doc), and when the policy is `ask`, it offers the command and waits. Nothing in that chain requires the runtime to expand a slash command, which is why it survives Devin and every future runtime.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md:18:- Topic: How should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime? Work through the ten research angles in section 3 of specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md: inventory, scoring, output contract, run or ask, invocation mechanics, chat-only users, skill and command linkage, measurement, prior art, failure modes. Start from the advisor runtime in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor (command-bridges, scorer projection and fusion, render.ts), the commands tree, AGENTS.md gates 2 and 4, and the prior packets 003-doctor-command-surfacing and system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review. Cite path:line for every claim and name evidence that contradicts a recommendation as well as evidence that supports it.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md:58:- [x] Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md:100:- \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one. (iteration 5)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md:24:5. Even a typed slash command ranks the owning *skill* above the bridge: `/deep:research` boosts `[['system-deep-loop', 1.6], ['command-spec-kit', 0.45]]`, `/deep:review` the same, and `/speckit:resume` boosts `[['system-spec-kit', 0.9], ['command-spec-kit', 0.75]]` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:97]. The typed-command path therefore *is* a skill recommendation by construction; the bridge id surfaces only as a lower-weight runner-up, which is what the spec's brief shows as a bare `command-spec-kit` [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:34].\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:66:      \"text\": \"Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:174:      \"text\": \"Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:411:      \"text\": \"Even a typed slash command ranks the owning *skill* above the bridge: `/deep:research` boosts `[['system-deep-loop', 1.6], ['command-spec-kit', 0.45]]`, `/deep:review` the same, and `/speckit:resume` boosts `[['system-spec-kit', 0.9], ['command-spec-kit', 0.75]]` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts:97]. The typed-command path therefore *is* a skill recommendation by construction; the bridge id surfaces only as a lower-weight runner-up, which is what the spec's brief shows as a bare `command-spec-kit` [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:34].\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:633:      \"text\": \"There is no `kind` and no runnable-command field anywhere in the public response; the only command-adjacent field is the optional `workflowMode`, which names a hub mode rather than a slash command [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:307]. The internal `AdvisorRecommendation.kind` seen in iteration 2 is dropped at this boundary because it is optional and not in the schema [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:41].\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:793:      \"text\": \"No model-facing rule anywhere instructs the model to type a slash command. `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 tells the model to use the hook brief and to run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend …`, and its output line is `SKILL ROUTING: …` [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:69]. The deep-research skill states it \\\"is invoked exclusively through `/deep:research:auto` or `/deep:research:confirm`\\\" — a statement about user entry, not model entry [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:1].\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:832:      \"text\": \"The repository already has a precedent for the model executing an *entry point it was told about*: the advisor's outage fallback prints the literal `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"<request>\\\"}' --format json` line, expecting the model to run it [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:590]. The precedent covers shell entry points, not slash commands.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:1225:      \"text\": \"Prior art from outside this repository, marked as inference because no external page was fetched in this session: agent harnesses expose slash commands as user-invoked entries, not model-callable tools, and the `AGENTS.md` convention exists precisely so one instruction file can serve several harnesses [INFERENCE: from the per-runtime mirrors above plus the absence of any model-invoked command surface in seven adapters].\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/findings-registry.json:1469:      \"text\": \"\\\"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\\\": no runtime exposes slash commands as model tools, and no repository rule instructs the model to type one.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md:17:2. There is no `kind` and no runnable-command field anywhere in the public response; the only command-adjacent field is the optional `workflowMode`, which names a hub mode rather than a slash command [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:307]. The internal `AdvisorRecommendation.kind` seen in iteration 2 is dropped at this boundary because it is optional and not in the schema [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:41].\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n --no-heading \"cannot (run|invoke|start).*slash|slash command.*(invoke|start|run)|model.*slash command|slash command.*model|commands are user\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring --glob '*.md' --glob '*.json' | head -40","time":{"start":1794476864532,"end":1794476864571}},"id":"prt_1cf27f12e001p74BQqVIv166ir","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf27d938001tNNyumQwXwZAmP"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476864977,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_zij49sksnms9sh1d1r1xbjdh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json; echo \"---CAP-DOC---\"; sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md 2>/dev/null","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\",\n  \"docPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md\",\n  \"resolverScript\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"runtimes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"opencode\",\n      \"label\": \"OpenCode / Copilot\",\n      \"mirrorPath\": \".skilled/agents/deep-research.md\",\n      \"toolSurface\": [\n        \"Read\",\n        \"Write\",\n        \"Edit\",\n        \"Bash\",\n        \"Grep\",\n        \"Glob\",\n        \"WebFetch\",\n        \"memory\"\n      ],\n      \"hookBootstrap\": false,\n      \"schemaAdaptation\": \"low\",\n      \"fallbackBridgeEligible\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"claude\",\n      \"label\": \"Claude\",\n      \"mirrorPath\": \".claude/agents/deep-research.md\",\n      \"toolSurface\": [\n        \"Read\",\n        \"Write\",\n        \"Edit\",\n        \"Bash\",\n        \"Grep\",\n        \"Glob\",\n        \"WebFetch\",\n        \"memory\"\n      ],\n      \"hookBootstrap\": true,\n      \"schemaAdaptation\": \"low\",\n      \"fallbackBridgeEligible\": true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n---CAP-DOC---\n---\ntitle: Runtime Capability Matrix\ndescription: Single source of truth for deep-research runtime parity, lifecycle guarantees, and provider adaptation requirements.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"runtime capability matrix\"\n  - \"deep research runtime parity\"\n  - \"provider adaptation rules\"\n  - \"non-hook equivalence\"\n  - \"research parity baseline\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.1.0\n---\n\n# Runtime Capability Matrix\n\nCanonical runtime parity reference for deep-research mirrors and provider adaptation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nCanonical runtime contract for `deep-research`. This matrix defines what every runtime mirror must support and what the workflow may adapt per provider. Packet files remain the source of truth; runtime behavior may differ only where this matrix says it may differ.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this matrix when adding or auditing a runtime mirror, or when deciding whether a provider difference is allowed adaptation or forbidden drift.\n\n### Machine-Readable Source of Truth\n\n- Data: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n- Resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n\n---\n\n## 2. PARITY BASELINE\n\nEvery runtime mirror for `@deep-research` must preserve these invariants:\n\n1. LEAF-only execution. No sub-agent dispatch.\n2. Canonical packet paths under `{spec_folder}/research/`, especially `research/deep-research-state.jsonl` and `research/findings-registry.json`.\n3. Lifecycle vocabulary: `resume`, `restart`, `fork`, `completed-continue`.\n4. Reducer-owned synchronization of strategy, dashboard, findings registry, and synthesis metadata.\n5. Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`.\n6. Lineage metadata keys: `sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`, `continuedFromRun`.\n\nIf any mirror drifts on those invariants, treat it as a contract failure rather than a runtime-specific customization.\n\n---\n\n## 3. MATRIX\n\n| Runtime | Mirror Path | Tool Surface | Hook Bootstrap | Schema Adaptation | Fallback Bridge Eligible | Notes |\n|---------|-------------|--------------|----------------|-------------------|--------------------------|-------|\n| OpenCode / Copilot | `.opencode/agents/deep-research.md` | `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Bash`, `Grep`, `Glob`, `WebFetch`, memory | No | Low | Yes | The runtime capability matrix sets `hookBootstrap: false` for the `.opencode` mirror; do not infer a plugin or Copilot hook from this packet. |\n| Claude | `.claude/agents/deep-research.md` | `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Bash`, `Grep`, `Glob`, `WebFetch`, MCP memory | Yes | Low | Yes | Default command YAML example path points here, but behavior is runtime-agnostic. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. ADAPTATION RULES\n\nAllowed runtime adaptation:\n\n- Tool names and transport details may change per runtime.\n- Provider-specific request formatting may change.\n- Hook-based startup ergonomics may change.\n\nForbidden runtime drift:\n\n- Renaming packet artifacts.\n- Changing lifecycle branch meaning.\n- Letting agent mirrors own reducer outputs.\n- Treating logs or traces as the source of truth instead of packet files.\n\n---\n\n## 5. NON-HOOK EQUIVALENCE\n\nHook-capable and non-hook runtimes must reach the same branch decision when given the same packet files:\n\n- Active packet -> `resume`\n- Completed packet reopened -> `completed-continue`\n- Explicit user reset -> `restart`\n- Explicit branch-from-current-state -> `fork`\n\nThe packet, not the hook state, decides the branch.\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION TARGETS\n\nUse this matrix as the parity checklist for validation:\n\n- Each mirror mentions the same canonical packet files.\n- Each mirror mentions reducer-owned synchronization.\n- Each mirror mentions the same lineage keys.\n- Each mirror preserves LEAF-only enforcement.\n- Each mirror treats `research/.deep-research-pause` as the only pause sentinel.\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\",\n  \"docPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md\",\n  \"resolverScript\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"runtimes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"opencode\",\n      \"label\": \"OpenCode / Copilot\",\n      \"mirrorPath\": \".skilled/agents/deep-research.md\",\n      \"toolSurface\": [\n        \"Read\",\n        \"Write\",\n        \"Edit\",\n        \"Bash\",\n        \"Grep\",\n        \"Glob\",\n        \"WebFetch\",\n        \"memory\"\n      ],\n      \"hookBootstrap\": false,\n      \"schemaAdaptation\": \"low\",\n      \"fallbackBridgeEligible\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"claude\",\n      \"label\": \"Claude\",\n      \"mirrorPath\": \".claude/agents/deep-research.md\",\n      \"toolSurface\": [\n        \"Read\",\n        \"Write\",\n        \"Edit\",\n        \"Bash\",\n        \"Grep\",\n        \"Glob\",\n        \"WebFetch\",\n        \"memory\"\n      ],\n      \"hookBootstrap\": true,\n      \"schemaAdaptation\": \"low\",\n      \"fallbackBridgeEligible\": true\n    }\n  ]\n}\n---CAP-DOC---\n---\ntitle: Runtime Capability Matrix\ndescription: Single source of truth for deep-research runtime parity, lifecycle guarantees, and provider adaptation requirements.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"runtime capability matrix\"\n  - \"deep research runtime parity\"\n  - \"provider adaptation rules\"\n  - \"non-hook equivalence\"\n  - \"research parity baseline\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.14.1.0\n---\n\n# Runtime Capability Matrix\n\nCanonical runtime parity reference for deep-research mirrors and provider adaptation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nCanonical runtime contract for `deep-research`. This matrix defines what every runtime mirror must support and what the workflow may adapt per provider. Packet files remain the source of truth; runtime behavior may differ only where this matrix says it may differ.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this matrix when adding or auditing a runtime mirror, or when deciding whether a provider difference is allowed adaptation or forbidden drift.\n\n### Machine-Readable Source of Truth\n\n- Data: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n- Resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n\n---\n\n## 2. PARITY BASELINE\n\nEvery runtime mirror for `@deep-research` must preserve these invariants:\n\n1. LEAF-only execution. No sub-agent dispatch.\n2. Canonical packet paths under `{spec_folder}/research/`, especially `research/deep-research-state.jsonl` and `research/findings-registry.json`.\n3. Lifecycle vocabulary: `resume`, `restart`, `fork`, `completed-continue`.\n4. Reducer-owned synchronization of strategy, dashboard, findings registry, and synthesis metadata.\n5. Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`.\n6. Lineage metadata keys: `sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`, `continuedFromRun`.\n\nIf any mirror drifts on those invariants, treat it as a contract failure rather than a runtime-specific customization.\n\n---\n\n## 3. MATRIX\n\n| Runtime | Mirror Path | Tool Surface | Hook Bootstrap | Schema Adaptation | Fallback Bridge Eligible | Notes |\n|---------|-------------|--------------|----------------|-------------------|--------------------------|-------|\n| OpenCode / Copilot | `.opencode/agents/deep-research.md` | `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Bash`, `Grep`, `Glob`, `WebFetch`, memory | No | Low | Yes | The runtime capability matrix sets `hookBootstrap: false` for the `.opencode` mirror; do not infer a plugin or Copilot hook from this packet. |\n| Claude | `.claude/agents/deep-research.md` | `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Bash`, `Grep`, `Glob`, `WebFetch`, MCP memory | Yes | Low | Yes | Default command YAML example path points here, but behavior is runtime-agnostic. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. ADAPTATION RULES\n\nAllowed runtime adaptation:\n\n- Tool names and transport details may change per runtime.\n- Provider-specific request formatting may change.\n- Hook-based startup ergonomics may change.\n\nForbidden runtime drift:\n\n- Renaming packet artifacts.\n- Changing lifecycle branch meaning.\n- Letting agent mirrors own reducer outputs.\n- Treating logs or traces as the source of truth instead of packet files.\n\n---\n\n## 5. NON-HOOK EQUIVALENCE\n\nHook-capable and non-hook runtimes must reach the same branch decision when given the same packet files:\n\n- Active packet -> `resume`\n- Completed packet reopened -> `completed-continue`\n- Explicit user reset -> `restart`\n- Explicit branch-from-current-state -> `fork`\n\nThe packet, not the hook state, decides the branch.\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION TARGETS\n\nUse this matrix as the parity checklist for validation:\n\n- Each mirror mentions the same canonical packet files.\n- Each mirror mentions reducer-owned synchronization.\n- Each mirror mentions the same lineage keys.\n- Each mirror preserves LEAF-only enforcement.\n- Each mirror treats `research/.deep-research-pause` as the only pause sentinel.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json; echo \"---CAP-DOC---\"; sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md 2>/dev/null","time":{"start":1794476864945,"end":1794476864971}},"id":"prt_1cf27f42f001auIoP12FMtbamo","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf27d938001tNNyumQwXwZAmP"}}
