{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476896618,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_fvvm3y8eb6r17akir5lz5xyc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"commands are invoked\\|slash commands\" .skilled/commands/README.txt | head -5; echo \"---DEVIN---\"; ls .devin 2>/dev/null; echo \"---COMMAND-DOC-ENTRY---\"; sed -n '1,12p' .skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/commands/README.txt:3:description: \"OpenCode slash commands: component creation, deep loops, prompts, continuity and spec kit workflows.\"\n.skilled/commands/README.txt:6:  - \"slash commands\"\n.skilled/commands/README.txt:19:Commands are invoked as slash commands (e.g., `/create:feature-catalog`, `/deep:review`, `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:plan`). Each command is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter that defines its description, argument hints, and allowed tools.\n---DEVIN---\nagents\nconfig.json\nhooks\nhooks.v1.json\nmanual-testing-playbook\nmcp_config.json\nREADME.md\nrepo-rules\nskills\nSYNC.md\n---COMMAND-DOC-ENTRY---\n---\ndescription: \"Tune and rebuild the skill advisor, and audit graph freshness, router reach, budgets and parent hubs.\"\nargument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: system-skill-advisor -->\n\n# /doctor:skill-advisor Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It resolves the target and setup values from `_routes.yaml`, then loads the target workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n\n### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n","metadata":{"output":".skilled/commands/README.txt:3:description: \"OpenCode slash commands: component creation, deep loops, prompts, continuity and spec kit workflows.\"\n.skilled/commands/README.txt:6:  - \"slash commands\"\n.skilled/commands/README.txt:19:Commands are invoked as slash commands (e.g., `/create:feature-catalog`, `/deep:review`, `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:plan`). Each command is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter that defines its description, argument hints, and allowed tools.\n---DEVIN---\nagents\nconfig.json\nhooks\nhooks.v1.json\nmanual-testing-playbook\nmcp_config.json\nREADME.md\nrepo-rules\nskills\nSYNC.md\n---COMMAND-DOC-ENTRY---\n---\ndescription: \"Tune and rebuild the skill advisor, and audit graph freshness, router reach, budgets and parent hubs.\"\nargument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: system-skill-advisor -->\n\n# /doctor:skill-advisor Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It resolves the target and setup values from `_routes.yaml`, then loads the target workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n\n### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"commands are invoked\\|slash commands\" .skilled/commands/README.txt | head -5; echo \"---DEVIN---\"; ls .devin 2>/dev/null; echo \"---COMMAND-DOC-ENTRY---\"; sed -n '1,12p' .skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md","time":{"start":1794476896584,"end":1794476896617}},"id":"prt_1cf286f790011sR10aUTYUozQZ","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf2857a7001R7CgtttamZmV1Q"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476896817,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_5cxtxfw5ltgqdhmukn9deyoj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"for d in .claude/commands .opencode/commands .cursor/commands .codex/prompts .pi/prompts .dsh/prompts .devin; do if [ -e \"$d\" ]; then n=$(find -L \"$d\" -name \"*.md\" 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' '); echo \"$d: $n md files\"; else echo \"$d: MISSING\"; fi; done; echo \"---GATE4---\"; sed -n '87,92p' AGENTS.md; echo \"---HOOK-TABLE---\"; sed -n '45,65p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".claude/commands: 45 md files\n.opencode/commands: 91 md files\n.cursor/commands: 46 md files\n.codex/prompts: 45 md files\n.pi/prompts: 46 md files\n.dsh/prompts: 45 md files\n.devin: 12223 md files\n---GATE4---\nTrigger-phrase routing is Gate 2's, deep-loop state discipline the deep-mode `SKILL.md`'s; both fire before the owning skill loads:\n- **Executor CLI ≠ skill route.** \"Use cli-opencode gpt-5.5 high\" is the HOW: it runs inside the skill's workflow and never overrides the skill-owned route.\n- **Skill advisor ambiguity.** When the advisor's `command-spec-kit` bridge, keyed to `/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:resume`, `/deep:research` and `/deep:review`, matches alongside `cli-*` for iteration phrases, `command-spec-kit` wins.\n\n#### GATE 5: REPO RULES LOAD [HARD] BLOCK\nTrigger: the FIRST write of the session, in any repository whose root holds a `REPO RULES.md`. Read-only turns never fire it; where that file is absent this document alone governs.\n---HOOK-TABLE---\n---\n\n## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n\nEvery native runtime and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n\n| Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n| **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n| **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n| **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n| **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, `.pi/extensions/` symlinks here) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n| **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n\nOpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n\n---\n\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n","metadata":{"output":".claude/commands: 45 md files\n.opencode/commands: 91 md files\n.cursor/commands: 46 md files\n.codex/prompts: 45 md files\n.pi/prompts: 46 md files\n.dsh/prompts: 45 md files\n.devin: 12223 md files\n---GATE4---\nTrigger-phrase routing is Gate 2's, deep-loop state discipline the deep-mode `SKILL.md`'s; both fire before the owning skill loads:\n- **Executor CLI ≠ skill route.** \"Use cli-opencode gpt-5.5 high\" is the HOW: it runs inside the skill's workflow and never overrides the skill-owned route.\n- **Skill advisor ambiguity.** When the advisor's `command-spec-kit` bridge, keyed to `/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:resume`, `/deep:research` and `/deep:review`, matches alongside `cli-*` for iteration phrases, `command-spec-kit` wins.\n\n#### GATE 5: REPO RULES LOAD [HARD] BLOCK\nTrigger: the FIRST write of the session, in any repository whose root holds a `REPO RULES.md`. Read-only turns never fire it; where that file is absent this document alone governs.\n---HOOK-TABLE---\n---\n\n## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n\nEvery native runtime and Pi run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n\n| Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n| **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n| **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n| **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n| **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, `.pi/extensions/` symlinks here) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n| **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n\nOpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n\n---\n\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"for d in .claude/commands .opencode/commands .cursor/commands .codex/prompts .pi/prompts .dsh/prompts .devin; do if [ -e \"$d\" ]; then n=$(find -L \"$d\" -name \"*.md\" 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' '); echo \"$d: $n md files\"; else echo \"$d: MISSING\"; fi; done; echo \"---GATE4---\"; sed -n '87,92p' AGENTS.md; echo \"---HOOK-TABLE---\"; sed -n '45,65p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","time":{"start":1794476896083,"end":1794476896816}},"id":"prt_1cf286cbe001Bpt9coMgADzt6F","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf2857a7001R7CgtttamZmV1Q"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794476898735,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"id":"prt_1cf2879ad001u11DHcAUTPhE9u","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"32334c1be320f36038cc99d774ef482e874dcd66","messageID":"msg_1cf2857a7001R7CgtttamZmV1Q","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":225454,"input":3353,"output":370,"reasoning":163,"cache":{"write":0,"read":221568}},"cost":0.001487454}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794476904887,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"id":"prt_1cf2891b5001YCSZl72kMscDnz","messageID":"msg_1cf287fdc001DtWsOM3Cdo0Nrg","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","snapshot":"b0bf93a56d2fe16b07218af47548d1e22196b344","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476916658,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_nlzd51fyymkzc4wozri7lqfm","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: Invocation mechanics across seven runtimes\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 5 (invocation mechanics): whether a model can start a slash command itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot. The selected interpretation is model-initiated workflow execution, not user-typed invocation.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Counted the command surface in every runtime mirror in this worktree.\n- Checked the command tree's own definition of how commands are invoked.\n- Checked the model-facing routing rules in `AGENTS.md` for any instruction to type a slash command.\n- Checked the advisor's fallback directive for the repository's one model-executable precedent.\n- Read the per-runtime delivery table in the advisor hook reference.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. Every runtime except Devin mirrors the command tree into a user-facing slash surface, in different shapes: `.claude/commands` holds 45 markdown files in group directories, `.opencode/commands` symlinks the source group directories, `.cursor/commands` holds 46 flat files, `.codex/prompts` 45, `.pi/prompts` 46, and `.dsh/prompts` 45. `.devin` contains agents, hooks, skills and repo-rules but no commands or prompts directory. [SOURCE: .claude/commands:1] [SOURCE: .opencode/commands:1] [SOURCE: .devin/SYNC.md:1]\n\n2. The command tree defines commands as user-invoked: \"Commands are invoked as slash commands ... Each command is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter that defines its description, argument hints, and allowed tools.\" The definition names no model-callable surface. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/README.txt:19]\n\n3. The model-facing routing rule in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 tells the model to use the hook brief or run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend ...` and to emit `SKILL ROUTING: ...`; it never tells the model to type a slash command. Gate 4 names the `command-spec-kit` bridge as a tiebreak, again not as an invocation. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63] [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:90]\n\n4. The one model-executable precedent in the advisor is the outage fallback, which prints `route by hand: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"<request>\"}' --format json` for the model to run. The precedent covers a shell entry point, not a slash command. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:590]\n\n5. A command file is a thin router of plain repository markdown: for example `.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md` resolves a target from `_routes.yaml` and loads a target workflow YAML. A model that can read files and run tools can therefore execute the workflow without the runtime expanding a slash. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md:12]\n\n6. Two fallbacks cover every runtime: (a) name the command and ask the user to type it, which requires a user-facing slash surface; (b) load the command document and follow its workflow, which works on all seven runtimes including Devin because it needs only file reads and the model's ordinary tools. [INFERENCE: from findings 1-5]\n\n7. The delivery channel is not the constraint: the advisor already delivers a brief on Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, DSH, OpenCode and Pi through one shared renderer, while the command mirrors exist on six of those seven runtimes. The missing piece is a model-callable command entry, not a context channel. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:53]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"Give the model the slash string and it will invoke it\": the command docs are user-invoked, no tool schema exposes a slash command, and no model-facing rule instructs typing one.\n- Treating Devin as a delivery exception: it receives the brief and can load and follow a command doc; it simply has no slash surface for the user.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching for a model-invocable command mechanism in the hook adapters: they inject context or notices, and none can dispatch a command.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"start a slash command\" could mean user-typed invocation or model-initiated workflow execution; the selected interpretation is model-initiated execution.\n- Contradictory evidence: the command docs call commands user-invoked while the advisor tells the model about bridges; both are true at different layers, and the contradiction is resolved by the load-and-follow fallback.\n- Missing dependencies: Devin has no command surface to observe, so its behavior is inferred from its mirror contents and its hook configuration.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.claude/commands`, `.opencode/commands`, `.cursor/commands`, `.codex/prompts`, `.pi/prompts`, `.dsh/prompts`, `.devin`\n- `.skilled/commands/README.txt:19`\n- `AGENTS.md:63-69,90`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:590`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:53`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md:1-12`\n- Prior packet lineage `pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md` (same packet, cross-checked against the tree)\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.5\n- Questions addressed: Can a model start a slash command itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what is the fallback where it cannot?\n- Questions answered: Can a model start a slash command itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what is the fallback where it cannot?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: counting the mirrors and reading the command tree's own invocation sentence turned a capability question into a structural one; if no runtime exposes a command tool, the fallback must be file-based.\n- What did not work and why: an initial `.devin` file count was inflated by nested skill content; the directory listing, not the count, established that Devin has no command surface.\n- What I would do differently: test the load-and-follow path on one command end to end, which would turn the inference into an observed behavior.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 6 (chat-only users): which mechanism brings a request typed as plain chat onto the command workflow, and what is the evidence that workflows are hand-rolled today.\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","time":{"start":1794476916650,"end":1794476916658}},"id":"prt_1cf28a4750017UQsZVlDcdXodh","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf287fdc001DtWsOM3Cdo0Nrg"}}
