{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476984398,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_ztl7n4q28cres9ukocz92tqq","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node -e 'const r=require(\"./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json\");console.log(JSON.stringify(r.advisorRoutingContract,null,1));console.log(\"---MODE---\");console.log(JSON.stringify(r.modes?.find(m=>m.command===\"/create:skill\")||r.modes?.[0],null,1).slice(0,1200));'","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"{\n \"routingClass\": \"metadata = resolved by hub membership (default for all sk-doc modes); command-bridge = reached only via its command, never advisor-scored. No lexical/alias-fold modes (avoids the advisor-projection extension + CI drift-guard).\",\n \"command\": \"The bound slash command for the mode, recorded even on metadata-routed modes; null when the mode has no dedicated command today.\",\n \"packetSkillName\": \"The packet SKILL.md name; folder == packetSkillName unless grandfatheredFolderMismatch is true.\",\n \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": \"false for every sk-doc mode (all folders are clean create-*/ names).\"\n}\n---MODE---\n{\n \"workflowMode\": \"sk-create-skill\",\n \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n \"backendKind\": \"template-scaffold\",\n \"toolSurface\": {\n  \"allowed\": [\n   \"Read\",\n   \"Write\",\n   \"Edit\",\n   \"Bash\",\n   \"Grep\",\n   \"Glob\"\n  ],\n  \"forbidden\": [\n   \"Task\"\n  ],\n  \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n  \"bashAllowlist\": []\n },\n \"packet\": \"sk-create-skill\",\n \"packetSkillName\": \"sk-create-skill\",\n \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n \"command\": \"/create:skill\",\n \"aliases\": [\n  \"create skill\",\n  \"new skill\",\n  \"skill scaffold\",\n  \"opencode skill\",\n  \"package skill\"\n ],\n \"advisorRouting\": {\n  \"routingClass\": \"metadata\"\n }\n}\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n \"routingClass\": \"metadata = resolved by hub membership (default for all sk-doc modes); command-bridge = reached only via its command, never advisor-scored. No lexical/alias-fold modes (avoids the advisor-projection extension + CI drift-guard).\",\n \"command\": \"The bound slash command for the mode, recorded even on metadata-routed modes; null when the mode has no dedicated command today.\",\n \"packetSkillName\": \"The packet SKILL.md name; folder == packetSkillName unless grandfatheredFolderMismatch is true.\",\n \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": \"false for every sk-doc mode (all folders are clean create-*/ names).\"\n}\n---MODE---\n{\n \"workflowMode\": \"sk-create-skill\",\n \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n \"backendKind\": \"template-scaffold\",\n \"toolSurface\": {\n  \"allowed\": [\n   \"Read\",\n   \"Write\",\n   \"Edit\",\n   \"Bash\",\n   \"Grep\",\n   \"Glob\"\n  ],\n  \"forbidden\": [\n   \"Task\"\n  ],\n  \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n  \"bashAllowlist\": []\n },\n \"packet\": \"sk-create-skill\",\n \"packetSkillName\": \"sk-create-skill\",\n \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n \"command\": \"/create:skill\",\n \"aliases\": [\n  \"create skill\",\n  \"new skill\",\n  \"skill scaffold\",\n  \"opencode skill\",\n  \"package skill\"\n ],\n \"advisorRouting\": {\n  \"routingClass\": \"metadata\"\n }\n}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"node -e 'const r=require(\"./.skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json\");console.log(JSON.stringify(r.advisorRoutingContract,null,1));console.log(\"---MODE---\");console.log(JSON.stringify(r.modes?.find(m=>m.command===\"/create:skill\")||r.modes?.[0],null,1).slice(0,1200));'","time":{"start":1794476984346,"end":1794476984397}},"id":"prt_1cf29c65e001QafZWJib1GvgbC","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf29b457001N3OPRX4cQCr1B7"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794476984805,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_dywitvlxm6fy3651zuy3o7w4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node -e 'const r=require(\"./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json\");console.log(JSON.stringify(r.advisorRoutingContract,null,1));console.log(\"---MODE---\");console.log(JSON.stringify(r.modes?.find(m=>m.command===\"/deep:research\")||r.modes?.[0],null,1).slice(0,1200));'","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"{\n \"routingClass\": \"How the advisor finds the mode. 'lexical' = weighted-regex scoring in skill_advisor.py AND present in both projection maps. 'alias-fold' = TS DEEP_MODE_BY_CANONICAL only (alias projection, not lexically scored). 'metadata' = resolved by skill membership; no advisor map entry. 'command-bridge' = routed by its /deep:* command, not an advisor map entry.\",\n \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"The legacy deep-* skill id the projection maps key on (present for lexical + alias-fold modes only).\",\n \"advisorDefaultMode\": \"Marks the default mode a multi-mode legacy id folds to. Never inferred from array order.\",\n \"legacyAliases\": \"The TypeScript scorer alias set (aliases.ts SKILL_ALIAS_GROUPS[legacyAdvisorId]) the merged-identity layer keys on; the drift-guard asserts these match it order-insensitive. The Python deep-router uses its own alias set + regex patterns by design (same keys, different values), so the guard only cross-checks that each legacyAdvisorId key also exists in the Python SKILL_ALIAS_GROUPS.\",\n \"packetSkillName\": \"The packet's SKILL.md name. Most packets use folder == packetSkillName == deep-<mode> (e.g. deep-ai-council). The legacy public key 'ai-council' is preserved only on the command/agent surfaces, not on the packet folder/name.\",\n \"driftGuard\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/routing-registry-drift-guard.vitest.ts\"\n}\n---MODE---\n{\n \"workflowMode\": \"research\",\n \"runtimeLoopType\": \"research\",\n \"backendKind\": \"runtime-loop-type\",\n \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n \"toolSurface\": {\n  \"allowed\": [\n   \"Read\",\n   \"Write\",\n   \"Edit\",\n   \"Bash\",\n   \"Grep\",\n   \"Glob\",\n   \"Task\",\n   \"WebFetch\"\n  ],\n  \"forbidden\": [],\n  \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n  \"bashAllowlist\": []\n },\n \"packet\": \"deep-research\",\n \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-research\",\n \"command\": \"/deep:research\",\n \"agent\": \"deep-research\",\n \"artifactRoot\": \"research/\",\n \"aliases\": [\n  \"deep-research\",\n  \"research loop\",\n  \"iterative investigation workflow\",\n  \"research convergence detection\",\n  \"autoresearch\",\n  \"iterative-research\"\n ],\n \"advisorRouting\": {\n  \"routingClass\": \"lexical\",\n  \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"deep-research\",\n  \"legacyAliases\": [\n   \"command-spec-kit-deep-research\",\n   \"/deep:research\",\n   \"spec_kit:deep-research\",\n   \"deep-research\",\n   \"sk-deep-research\"\n  ]\n }\n}\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n \"routingClass\": \"How the advisor finds the mode. 'lexical' = weighted-regex scoring in skill_advisor.py AND present in both projection maps. 'alias-fold' = TS DEEP_MODE_BY_CANONICAL only (alias projection, not lexically scored). 'metadata' = resolved by skill membership; no advisor map entry. 'command-bridge' = routed by its /deep:* command, not an advisor map entry.\",\n \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"The legacy deep-* skill id the projection maps key on (present for lexical + alias-fold modes only).\",\n \"advisorDefaultMode\": \"Marks the default mode a multi-mode legacy id folds to. Never inferred from array order.\",\n \"legacyAliases\": \"The TypeScript scorer alias set (aliases.ts SKILL_ALIAS_GROUPS[legacyAdvisorId]) the merged-identity layer keys on; the drift-guard asserts these match it order-insensitive. The Python deep-router uses its own alias set + regex patterns by design (same keys, different values), so the guard only cross-checks that each legacyAdvisorId key also exists in the Python SKILL_ALIAS_GROUPS.\",\n \"packetSkillName\": \"The packet's SKILL.md name. Most packets use folder == packetSkillName == deep-<mode> (e.g. deep-ai-council). The legacy public key 'ai-council' is preserved only on the command/agent surfaces, not on the packet folder/name.\",\n \"driftGuard\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/routing-registry-drift-guard.vitest.ts\"\n}\n---MODE---\n{\n \"workflowMode\": \"research\",\n \"runtimeLoopType\": \"research\",\n \"backendKind\": \"runtime-loop-type\",\n \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n \"toolSurface\": {\n  \"allowed\": [\n   \"Read\",\n   \"Write\",\n   \"Edit\",\n   \"Bash\",\n   \"Grep\",\n   \"Glob\",\n   \"Task\",\n   \"WebFetch\"\n  ],\n  \"forbidden\": [],\n  \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n  \"bashAllowlist\": []\n },\n \"packet\": \"deep-research\",\n \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-research\",\n \"command\": \"/deep:research\",\n \"agent\": \"deep-research\",\n \"artifactRoot\": \"research/\",\n \"aliases\": [\n  \"deep-research\",\n  \"research loop\",\n  \"iterative investigation workflow\",\n  \"research convergence detection\",\n  \"autoresearch\",\n  \"iterative-research\"\n ],\n \"advisorRouting\": {\n  \"routingClass\": \"lexical\",\n  \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"deep-research\",\n  \"legacyAliases\": [\n   \"command-spec-kit-deep-research\",\n   \"/deep:research\",\n   \"spec_kit:deep-research\",\n   \"deep-research\",\n   \"sk-deep-research\"\n  ]\n }\n}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"node -e 'const r=require(\"./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json\");console.log(JSON.stringify(r.advisorRoutingContract,null,1));console.log(\"---MODE---\");console.log(JSON.stringify(r.modes?.find(m=>m.command===\"/deep:research\")||r.modes?.[0],null,1).slice(0,1200));'","time":{"start":1794476984762,"end":1794476984804}},"id":"prt_1cf29c83d001Ys2cidYnkZo8rY","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf29b457001N3OPRX4cQCr1B7"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794476986008,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"id":"prt_1cf29ce95001qofKSyl3O14Xkn","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"e694c860718d6216b417291f986e764acf3203ce","messageID":"msg_1cf29b457001N3OPRX4cQCr1B7","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":241025,"input":1758,"output":310,"reasoning":109,"cache":{"write":0,"read":238848}},"cost":0.001231644}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794476991104,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"id":"prt_1cf29e27d001iaJQTy6S7AWCQK","messageID":"msg_1cf29d2b9001Enzj5GQ0ZezWBg","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","snapshot":"e694c860718d6216b417291f986e764acf3203ce","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794477002148,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_ttfwlv0u8iajpgzh2wm1dwk1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 6: How a chat-only request reaches a command workflow\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 6 (chat-only users): which mechanism brings a request typed as plain chat onto the command workflow, and what is the evidence that workflows are hand-rolled today. The candidates are the advisor brief, an `AGENTS.md` gate, a hook, the skill pointing at its command, and a runner refusal.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Read the advisor hook reference's statement of what the brief is and is not.\n- Read the model-facing Gate 2 output contract and the PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK.\n- Read the runner-refusal prose in the deep-research skill.\n- Read the hub `mode-registry.json` files for the command-to-mode mapping.\n- Reused the measured zero-recommendation results from iteration 2.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The hook is advisory and fails open. It \"never replaces explicit skill loading, never persists raw prompt text, and never blocks the prompt on an advisor failure\", so a hook cannot redirect a chat request into a command by itself. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:21]\n\n2. The brief names recommended skills; only a doctor command appears as a runnable `/doctor:` string. A non-doctor command therefore has no model-visible invocation in the one prompt-time channel that reaches all runtimes. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:43]\n\n3. Gate 2 tells the model to use the brief or the advisor CLI and to emit `SKILL ROUTING: ...`; it never tells the model to run a command workflow. The ruleset routes to skills, so a chat-only request is steered toward a skill even when a command owns the workflow. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:69]\n\n4. The ruleset forbids hand-rolling a named workflow: PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK says \"NEVER silently hand-roll a substitute for a plan-named purpose-built workflow\". It says nothing about discovering that an unnamed command owns the request, so the prohibition cannot fire when the user typed prose. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:20] [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:27]\n\n5. The brief is silent exactly when a chat-only user needs it: the measured planning and research prompts return zero recommendations at the shipped 0.8 threshold, so there is no skill line and no command line to act on. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:43]\n\n6. A runner refusal exists only as normative prose. The deep-research skill says the loop \"is invoked exclusively through `/deep:research:auto` or `/deep:research:confirm`\" and never simulated with ad hoc dispatch, but that SKILL.md only loads after the skill has already been chosen, which is after the hand-roll decision. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:84]\n\n7. The hub mode registries already bind modes to commands, and are the authoritative linkage to use. `sk-doc` records a `command` for every mode (for example `/create:skill`) and states that a command-bridge mode is \"reached only via its command, never advisor-scored\"; `system-deep-loop` records `/deep:research` on the research mode with lexical routing. A command-aware brief can therefore be generated from existing registries rather than from a new list. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json:13] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:45]\n\n8. Recommended mechanism: the brief carries `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` from the hub registry, and `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 gains one rule: when the brief names a command whose policy is run, load that command document and execute its workflow; when the policy is ask, offer the command and wait. Rejected alternatives: a hook prompt rewrite (advisory-only and fail-open), a runner refusal (fires after skill selection), a skill that points at its command alone (requires the skill to load first and does not itself reach the model), and a static command list in `AGENTS.md` (45 entries that drift). [INFERENCE: from findings 1-7]\n\n9. Contradicting evidence: on a runtime where the brief does not arrive, the mechanism must still work, so the Gate 2 rule should also say \"if no brief arrived, ask the advisor CLI before hand-rolling\". The hook reference lists all seven runtimes, but delivery can fail open to the directives fallback, so the static rule is the backstop. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:21]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A hook-only mechanism: the hook is advisory and cannot dispatch a command.\n- A runner-refusal-only mechanism: the refusal text loads too late to prevent the hand-roll.\n- A static command list in `AGENTS.md`: 45 entries with modes and arguments would drift and consume the rule budget.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching the ruleset for an existing anti-hand-rolling discovery rule: only the substitution prohibition exists, and it presumes the workflow is named.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"chat-only\" could mean a runtime with no hooks; the selected interpretation is a user prompt with no slash command on any runtime, with the no-brief case handled as the backstop.\n- Contradictory evidence: the deep hub says skills and commands are complementary surfaces over the same packets, while sk-doc says command-bridge modes are reached only via their command. Both are true per hub, and the brief must carry the hub's own routing class.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:21,43`\n- `AGENTS.md:20-27,69`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md:84`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json:13,40`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:45`\n- `spec.md:43-47` (measured zero recommendations)\n- Prior packet lineage `pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md` (same packet, cross-checked)\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.6\n- Questions addressed: Which mechanism brings a request typed as plain chat onto the command workflow, and what is the evidence that workflows are hand-rolled today?\n- Questions answered: Which mechanism brings a request typed as plain chat onto the command workflow, and what is the evidence that workflows are hand-rolled today?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: the mode registries turned a design debate into a data question; the command already exists beside every mode, so the missing piece is exposure and a rule, not a new inventory.\n- What did not work and why: looking for a runner refusal as enforcement failed because the refusal is prose that loads after the routing decision.\n- What I would do differently: test the no-brief path on a runtime where the hook is disabled, to see whether the fallback directive gives the model enough to find the command.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 7 (skill and command linkage): which commands never load the mode SKILL.md their metadata names, which skills have no command front door, and whether a skill recommendation should imply its command.\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md","time":{"start":1794477002138,"end":1794477002146}},"id":"prt_1cf29ee180012mBQ5i9ilrzSOa","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf29d2b9001Enzj5GQ0ZezWBg"}}
