{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794477185542,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_tthczqpram0q155xxfwf1sr1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":8,\"run\":8,\"runId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Measurement for command surfacing\",\"findingsCount\":8,\"newInfoRatio\":0.8,\"noveltyJustification\":\"The corpus gap and the command-metric set are new; the doctor reach tool was already known from iteration 1, so the ratio is slightly discounted.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which benchmark and fixture rows are needed for every command group and for chat-style prompts, and which metrics separate a missed command from a wrongly started one?\",\"How do other agent harnesses route a free-text request to a packaged workflow, from their public documentation?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which benchmark and fixture rows are needed for every command group and for chat-style prompts, and which metrics separate a missed command from a wrongly started one?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Reusing the skill accuracy gate as the command gate\",\"Adding command rows to the calibration corpus\"],\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/labeled-prompts.jsonl\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/scorer-calibration-baseline.json\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-metadata-e2e.vitest.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridge-resolution-guard.vitest.ts\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T09:52:53Z\",\"durationMs\":68000,\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q-measurement\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Which fixtures and metrics separate a missed command from a wrongly started one\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-001\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Corpus has no per-command-group buckets\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-004\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Existing command tests are inventory tests, not behavior tests\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-007\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Six command metrics separate recall from unsafe runs\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter008-001\",\"source\":\"f-iter008-001\",\"target\":\"q-measurement\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter008-002\",\"source\":\"f-iter008-004\",\"target\":\"q-measurement\",\"relation\":\"CONTRADICTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter008-003\",\"source\":\"f-iter008-007\",\"target\":\"q-measurement\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-001\",\"label\":\"The labeled corpus has 195 rows across true_write, true_read_only, memory_save_resume, mixed_ambiguous, deep_loop_prompts and skill_routing_prompts; none is keyed to the six command groups, so create, design, doctor and prompt regressions have no direct row.\",\"iteration\":8,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/labeled-prompts.jsonl:1\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-002\",\"label\":\"The calibration baseline covers 200 rows with Brier 0.204829 and expected calibration error 0.138314, and measures skill confidence quality, not command surfacing.\",\"iteration\":8,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/scorer-calibration-baseline.json:5\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-003\",\"label\":\"The release gate is skill-level: holdoutTop1, per-skill accuracy and UNKNOWN counts; no schema field counts command recall, command precision, ask decisions or unsafe starts.\",\"iteration\":8,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:496\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-004\",\"label\":\"Existing command tests are inventory tests: command-metadata-e2e asserts projection and file existence, and command-bridge-resolution-guard asserts bridge slash ids resolve; neither measures what a prompt returns.\",\"iteration\":8,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-metadata-e2e.vitest.ts:52\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridge-resolution-guard.vitest.ts:1\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-005\",\"label\":\"The doctor family has the right proof shape: doctor-phrase-reach.cjs checks each admitted phrase reaches its route; no equivalent exists for the other five groups.\",\"iteration\":8,\"sources\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:36\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-006\",\"label\":\"A complete fixture set needs three row types per group: a plain-chat recall row, a near-miss discrimination row against a competing skill, and a read-only or refusal row that must not start a mutating command, plus chat-only, partial-slash, quoted-slash and child-session variants.\",\"iteration\":8,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/labeled-prompts.jsonl:1\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-007\",\"label\":\"The metrics that separate the failure classes are commandRecall@1 and commandPrecision, unsafeRunRate, askRecall and askPrecision, skillCommandAgreement and childAutoStartRate; a missed command is a recall failure with a silent brief and a wrongly started command is a precision or unsafe-run failure with a visible brief.\",\"iteration\":8,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:496\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter008-008\",\"label\":\"Command rows should live in a separate harness: the calibration Brier and ECE are tied to the 200-row corpus hash, so adding rows would make a routing regression look like a calibration change.\",\"iteration\":8,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/scorer-calibration-baseline.json:4\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Reusing the skill accuracy gate as the command gate\",\"reason\":\"It has no command class, so a command miss scores the same as a skill miss\",\"iteration\":8}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Adding command rows to the calibration corpus\",\"reason\":\"It would invalidate the corpus hash and the Brier/ECE baseline\",\"iteration\":8}\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-008.jsonl"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-008.jsonl","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-008.jsonl","time":{"start":1794477185536,"end":1794477185542}},"id":"prt_1cf2cc513001T2DRbgIbHq4p5d","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf2cb5fb001FccOjc5TMQxuuj"}}
