{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794477256831,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_0gknxn34schxzytvxg1yave2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":9,\"run\":9,\"runId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Prior art from public agent-harness documentation\",\"findingsCount\":9,\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"noveltyJustification\":\"The external evidence is new to this lineage and the host-frontmatter contradiction qualifies the recommendation; the convergence conclusion overlaps iteration 6, so the ratio is slightly discounted.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"How do other agent harnesses route a free-text request to a packaged workflow, from their public documentation?\",\"Which failure modes matter most: over-triggering, command-versus-skill ambiguity, a dispatched child session starting commands by itself, loops, and the brief budget?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"How do other agent harnesses route a free-text request to a packaged workflow, from their public documentation?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Copying Claude Code frontmatter directly as the repository mechanism\",\"A brief-only mechanism\"],\"edgeCase\":\"ambiguous-input\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"WebFetch\",\"WebSearch\",\"Read\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills\",\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/skills\",\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/custom-prompts\",\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/guides/agents-md\",\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/reference/slash-commands\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T09:54:05Z\",\"durationMs\":130000,\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q-prior-art\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"How do other harnesses route free text to a packaged workflow\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-002\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Claude Code exposes run-or-ask as skill frontmatter\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-005\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Codex deprecated custom prompts for skills\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-008\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Repository should mirror the metadata policy pattern\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter009-001\",\"source\":\"f-iter009-002\",\"target\":\"q-prior-art\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter009-002\",\"source\":\"f-iter009-005\",\"target\":\"q-prior-art\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter009-003\",\"source\":\"f-iter009-008\",\"target\":\"q-prior-art\",\"relation\":\"DERIVED_FROM\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-001\",\"label\":\"Claude Code presents one skill surface with two invocation paths: Claude uses skills when relevant, or the user invokes one directly with /skill-name; model invocation is the default.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-002\",\"label\":\"Claude Code exposes run-or-ask as skill frontmatter: disable-model-invocation true prevents automatic loading for side-effect workflows, and user-invocable false hides a skill from the user while keeping it model-invocable.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-003\",\"label\":\"The Agent SDK documentation states skills are model-invoked and user-invoked: Claude autonomously chooses based on context, or the user dispatches directly by sending /<name>.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/skills\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-004\",\"label\":\"Claude Code merged custom commands into skills: a command file and a skill both create /deploy, and existing command files keep working while skills add supporting files, invocation control and automatic loading.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-005\",\"label\":\"Codex deprecated custom prompts in favor of skills: custom prompts required explicit invocation and were not repo-shared, while skills can be invoked explicitly or implicitly.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/custom-prompts\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-006\",\"label\":\"Codex's durable instruction layer is AGENTS.md, described as persistent project guidance for every session and the portable place for repo rules.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/guides/agents-md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-007\",\"label\":\"The ChatGPT desktop app lists skills in the slash menu, allows explicit skill invocation, and exposes custom prompts as /prompts:<name>; the industry pattern is a model-invocable package plus a persistent instruction file.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/reference/slash-commands\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-008\",\"label\":\"The repository should mirror the platform pattern: command metadata carries an invocation policy equivalent to disable-model-invocation, the command document is the workflow body, and the brief only names the command and its policy.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills\",\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/custom-prompts\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter009-009\",\"label\":\"Host frontmatter is platform-specific: Claude Code reads .claude skill frontmatter while OpenCode, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH do not, so a repo-level policy must live in repository metadata and be rendered by the advisor.\",\"iteration\":9,\"sources\":[\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Copying Claude Code frontmatter directly as the repository mechanism\",\"reason\":\"Only one of seven runtimes reads it\",\"iteration\":9}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"A brief-only mechanism\",\"reason\":\"No reviewed harness uses a prompt-time brief as the primary route to a packaged workflow\",\"iteration\":9}\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-009.jsonl"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-009.jsonl","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-009.jsonl","time":{"start":1794477256822,"end":1794477256830}},"id":"prt_1cf2ddde8001JV0O4yE54idhFn","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf2dcb6e001gazJ15OxxleVln"}}
