{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794477280227,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_ulb6h61w0326d55frdrdhq39","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"AI_SESSION_CHILD\\|child-dispatch\\|Autonomous child-dispatch\" AGENTS.md | head -6; echo \"---AMBIGUITY---\"; sed -n '1,60p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts; echo \"---DOCTOR-AMBIG---\"; grep -n \"Doctor bridges must not shape\\|isPassingDoctorBridge\\|passingDoctorBridges\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts | head -10","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"84:- **Autonomous child-dispatch exemption.** `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` marks a non-interactive worker bound to a lineage directory. Gate 3 is PRE-RESOLVED; in that directory Law 4, Halt Conditions, Logic-Sync, Escalation and stop-for-yes are record-and-continue; acting outside it is barred. Interactive sessions always ask.\n111:Trigger: About to skip Gate 3, or realized it was skipped, on a turn where it fires and neither a session answer nor the child-dispatch exemption covers it → STOP → STATE: \"Before I proceed, I need to ask about documentation:\" → ASK Gate 3 (A/B/C/D) → WAIT. Any other skipped gate: run it before the next tool call.\n188:- **Do not ask permission to continue an already-approved, in-scope step.** This never waives a mandatory wait: Gate 3, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK approval, the worktree-versus-branch choice, the remote-push go-ahead and the blast-radius stop-for-yes all still block. The §2 child-dispatch exemption is the one exception.\n---AMBIGUITY---\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Advisor Ambiguity\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport type { AdvisorScoredRecommendation } from './types.js';\n\nexport const AMBIGUITY_MARGIN = 0.05;\nexport const AMBIGUITY_CONFIDENCE_MARGIN = 0.05;\n\n// Compute ambiguity from ranking `score` so the cluster aligns\n// with the score-based fusion ranking (top-two-by-confidence may not match\n// top-two-by-score).\n//\n// Also compute on `confidence` and union the two\n// clusters. Score-margin keeps ranking alignment; confidence-margin restores\n// the documented \"0.05 confidence window\" and catches\n// cross-domain prompts where confidence is near-tied (user-visible signal)\n// even when score gaps just exceed the score margin. A candidate is in the\n// ambiguity cluster when EITHER gap is within its respective 0.05 margin —\n// \"outside both margins\" is required to be unambiguously ranked.\n//\n// One exception: a skill the typed-command bound capped just below the top\n// (`heldBelow` names the top) sits close to it only because of that cap, and the\n// cap already ranked the pair from the user's own command. Counting that gap as\n// a tie would report the explicit command as a coin flip. Two skills close on\n// their own evidence still cluster.\n//\n// The confidence margin has one exception of its own: when the top earned its\n// confidence from its own evidence, a member whose confidence only reached a\n// floor clusters on the score margin alone.\n\nfunction clustersWithTop(\n  top: AdvisorScoredRecommendation,\n  recommendation: AdvisorScoredRecommendation,\n  applyFloorException: boolean,\n): boolean {\n  if (recommendation !== top && recommendation.heldBelow === top.skill) return false;\n  const scoreGap = Math.abs(top.score - recommendation.score);\n  if (scoreGap <= AMBIGUITY_MARGIN + Number.EPSILON) return true;\n  // A floor pins many unrelated skills to the same confidence, which is not a\n  // tie with a top that earned its confidence from its own evidence.\n  const floorOnlyMember = applyFloorException\n    && recommendation.confidenceFloored === true\n    && top.confidenceFloored !== true;\n  if (floorOnlyMember) return false;\n  return Math.abs(top.confidence - recommendation.confidence)\n    <= AMBIGUITY_CONFIDENCE_MARGIN + Number.EPSILON;\n}\n\nfunction ambiguousCluster(\n  recommendations: readonly AdvisorScoredRecommendation[],\n  applyFloorException = true,\n): AdvisorScoredRecommendation[] {\n  const passing = recommendations.filter((recommendation) => recommendation.passes_threshold);\n  const [top] = passing;\n  if (!top) return [];\n  return passing.filter((recommendation) => clustersWithTop(top, recommendation, applyFloorException));\n}\n\nexport function isAmbiguousTopTwo(recommendations: readonly AdvisorScoredRecommendation[]): boolean {\n---DOCTOR-AMBIG---\n914:  const isPassingDoctorBridge = (recommendation: AdvisorScoredRecommendation): boolean => (\n923:      if (!isPassingDoctorBridge(recommendation)) return;\n944:    if (!isPassingDoctorBridge(recommendation)) return false;\n963:  const passingDoctorBridges = ranked.filter(isPassingDoctorBridge);\n964:  if (passingDoctorBridges.length === 0) return [...ranked];\n965:  const remaining = ranked.filter((recommendation) => !isPassingDoctorBridge(recommendation));\n979:    ...passingDoctorBridges,\n1225:  // Doctor bridges must not shape skill ambiguity or abstention.\n","metadata":{"output":"84:- **Autonomous child-dispatch exemption.** `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` marks a non-interactive worker bound to a lineage directory. Gate 3 is PRE-RESOLVED; in that directory Law 4, Halt Conditions, Logic-Sync, Escalation and stop-for-yes are record-and-continue; acting outside it is barred. Interactive sessions always ask.\n111:Trigger: About to skip Gate 3, or realized it was skipped, on a turn where it fires and neither a session answer nor the child-dispatch exemption covers it → STOP → STATE: \"Before I proceed, I need to ask about documentation:\" → ASK Gate 3 (A/B/C/D) → WAIT. Any other skipped gate: run it before the next tool call.\n188:- **Do not ask permission to continue an already-approved, in-scope step.** This never waives a mandatory wait: Gate 3, PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK approval, the worktree-versus-branch choice, the remote-push go-ahead and the blast-radius stop-for-yes all still block. The §2 child-dispatch exemption is the one exception.\n---AMBIGUITY---\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Advisor Ambiguity\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport type { AdvisorScoredRecommendation } from './types.js';\n\nexport const AMBIGUITY_MARGIN = 0.05;\nexport const AMBIGUITY_CONFIDENCE_MARGIN = 0.05;\n\n// Compute ambiguity from ranking `score` so the cluster aligns\n// with the score-based fusion ranking (top-two-by-confidence may not match\n// top-two-by-score).\n//\n// Also compute on `confidence` and union the two\n// clusters. Score-margin keeps ranking alignment; confidence-margin restores\n// the documented \"0.05 confidence window\" and catches\n// cross-domain prompts where confidence is near-tied (user-visible signal)\n// even when score gaps just exceed the score margin. A candidate is in the\n// ambiguity cluster when EITHER gap is within its respective 0.05 margin —\n// \"outside both margins\" is required to be unambiguously ranked.\n//\n// One exception: a skill the typed-command bound capped just below the top\n// (`heldBelow` names the top) sits close to it only because of that cap, and the\n// cap already ranked the pair from the user's own command. Counting that gap as\n// a tie would report the explicit command as a coin flip. Two skills close on\n// their own evidence still cluster.\n//\n// The confidence margin has one exception of its own: when the top earned its\n// confidence from its own evidence, a member whose confidence only reached a\n// floor clusters on the score margin alone.\n\nfunction clustersWithTop(\n  top: AdvisorScoredRecommendation,\n  recommendation: AdvisorScoredRecommendation,\n  applyFloorException: boolean,\n): boolean {\n  if (recommendation !== top && recommendation.heldBelow === top.skill) return false;\n  const scoreGap = Math.abs(top.score - recommendation.score);\n  if (scoreGap <= AMBIGUITY_MARGIN + Number.EPSILON) return true;\n  // A floor pins many unrelated skills to the same confidence, which is not a\n  // tie with a top that earned its confidence from its own evidence.\n  const floorOnlyMember = applyFloorException\n    && recommendation.confidenceFloored === true\n    && top.confidenceFloored !== true;\n  if (floorOnlyMember) return false;\n  return Math.abs(top.confidence - recommendation.confidence)\n    <= AMBIGUITY_CONFIDENCE_MARGIN + Number.EPSILON;\n}\n\nfunction ambiguousCluster(\n  recommendations: readonly AdvisorScoredRecommendation[],\n  applyFloorException = true,\n): AdvisorScoredRecommendation[] {\n  const passing = recommendations.filter((recommendation) => recommendation.passes_threshold);\n  const [top] = passing;\n  if (!top) return [];\n  return passing.filter((recommendation) => clustersWithTop(top, recommendation, applyFloorException));\n}\n\nexport function isAmbiguousTopTwo(recommendations: readonly AdvisorScoredRecommendation[]): boolean {\n---DOCTOR-AMBIG---\n914:  const isPassingDoctorBridge = (recommendation: AdvisorScoredRecommendation): boolean => (\n923:      if (!isPassingDoctorBridge(recommendation)) return;\n944:    if (!isPassingDoctorBridge(recommendation)) return false;\n963:  const passingDoctorBridges = ranked.filter(isPassingDoctorBridge);\n964:  if (passingDoctorBridges.length === 0) return [...ranked];\n965:  const remaining = ranked.filter((recommendation) => !isPassingDoctorBridge(recommendation));\n979:    ...passingDoctorBridges,\n1225:  // Doctor bridges must not shape skill ambiguity or abstention.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"AI_SESSION_CHILD\\|child-dispatch\\|Autonomous child-dispatch\" AGENTS.md | head -6; echo \"---AMBIGUITY---\"; sed -n '1,60p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts; echo \"---DOCTOR-AMBIG---\"; grep -n \"Doctor bridges must not shape\\|isPassingDoctorBridge\\|passingDoctorBridges\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts | head -10","time":{"start":1794477280190,"end":1794477280226}},"id":"prt_1cf2e4990001q8FFisRFDZ2Fr6","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf2e23f7001csSHmV6J5i9ZN9"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794477281112,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_2vc6xlqevk06wdyr1cd3dj5t","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"loop\\|re-route\\|already routed\\|routing again\\|recursive\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md | head -20; echo \"---ADVISOR-PENALTY---\"; grep -n \"auditRecsAdvisorPenalty\\|ADVISOR_SELF_RECOMMENDATION\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts | head -10; echo \"---DIRECTIVE-DEDUP---\"; grep -n \"dedup\\|cadence\\|same-session\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | head -8","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"---ADVISOR-PENALTY---\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:97:const ADVISOR_SELF_RECOMMENDATION_SKILL_IDS = new Set(['system-skill-advisor', 'skill-advisor']);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:433:  return ADVISOR_SELF_RECOMMENDATION_SKILL_IDS.has(skillId);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:816:    if (isAdvisorSelfRecommendationSkill(recommendation.skill)) return R.auditRecsAdvisorPenalty;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts:157:  readonly auditRecsAdvisorPenalty: number;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts:237:    auditRecsAdvisorPenalty: -0.25,\n---DIRECTIVE-DEDUP---\n40:6. **Directive-lifecycle dedup.** `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` suppresses a re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence, so a repeated prompt does not re-inject an identical brief. A repeat in a known session keeps the first line, a route or a fallback status, and drops the directives block.\n57:| **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, `.pi/extensions/` symlinks here) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n58:| **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n97:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | The real advisor handler (Claude shape). Builds the brief, runs the CLI fallback, renders, applies directive-lifecycle dedup, emits the `additionalContext` envelope, persists a diagnostic record. The codex/cursor/devin siblings share the same advisor core over their runtime's payload shape. |\n99:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Native Pi extension. Imports the advisor module in-process, captures raw user text (bounded LRU), runs a delivery-state machine that suppresses same-session re-delivery, and sends the brief as a model-visible message. Races the advisor call against a deadline of the advisor budget plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directives if it hangs. |\n100:| `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | OpenCode plugin. `experimental.chat.system.transform` spawns the bridge and appends the brief to `output.system`. `event` manages session lifecycle and cache invalidation. `tool: spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` returns a sanitized status report. TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup and transform-dedup integration. |\n104:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | Directive-lifecycle dedup: decides whether a directive should be re-delivered to a session within its cadence. |\n137:| Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n","metadata":{"output":"---ADVISOR-PENALTY---\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:97:const ADVISOR_SELF_RECOMMENDATION_SKILL_IDS = new Set(['system-skill-advisor', 'skill-advisor']);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:433:  return ADVISOR_SELF_RECOMMENDATION_SKILL_IDS.has(skillId);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:816:    if (isAdvisorSelfRecommendationSkill(recommendation.skill)) return R.auditRecsAdvisorPenalty;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts:157:  readonly auditRecsAdvisorPenalty: number;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts:237:    auditRecsAdvisorPenalty: -0.25,\n---DIRECTIVE-DEDUP---\n40:6. **Directive-lifecycle dedup.** `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` suppresses a re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence, so a repeated prompt does not re-inject an identical brief. A repeat in a known session keeps the first line, a route or a fallback status, and drops the directives block.\n57:| **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, `.pi/extensions/` symlinks here) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n58:| **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n97:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | The real advisor handler (Claude shape). Builds the brief, runs the CLI fallback, renders, applies directive-lifecycle dedup, emits the `additionalContext` envelope, persists a diagnostic record. The codex/cursor/devin siblings share the same advisor core over their runtime's payload shape. |\n99:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Native Pi extension. Imports the advisor module in-process, captures raw user text (bounded LRU), runs a delivery-state machine that suppresses same-session re-delivery, and sends the brief as a model-visible message. Races the advisor call against a deadline of the advisor budget plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directives if it hangs. |\n100:| `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | OpenCode plugin. `experimental.chat.system.transform` spawns the bridge and appends the brief to `output.system`. `event` manages session lifecycle and cache invalidation. `tool: spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` returns a sanitized status report. TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup and transform-dedup integration. |\n104:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | Directive-lifecycle dedup: decides whether a directive should be re-delivered to a session within its cadence. |\n137:| Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"loop\\|re-route\\|already routed\\|routing again\\|recursive\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md | head -20; echo \"---ADVISOR-PENALTY---\"; grep -n \"auditRecsAdvisorPenalty\\|ADVISOR_SELF_RECOMMENDATION\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts | head -10; echo \"---DIRECTIVE-DEDUP---\"; grep -n \"dedup\\|cadence\\|same-session\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | head -8","time":{"start":1794477281069,"end":1794477281111}},"id":"prt_1cf2e4bd8001XzgTPSzKeDKX2J","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf2e23f7001csSHmV6J5i9ZN9"}}
