{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794477334190,"sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_z0nt3wa85qcfszrna1g3vlkc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":10,\"run\":10,\"runId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Failure modes and their controls\",\"findingsCount\":9,\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"noveltyJustification\":\"The child-authority and routing-loop findings are new; the ambiguity and over-trigger controls restate earlier measurements, so the ratio is discounted.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which failure modes matter most: over-triggering, command-versus-skill ambiguity, a dispatched child session starting commands by itself, loops, and the brief budget?\",\"Who owns the final recommendation set and what evidence would change each recommendation?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which failure modes matter most: over-triggering, command-versus-skill ambiguity, a dispatched child session starting commands by itself, loops, and the brief budget?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"A blanket command-first tiebreak\",\"Relying on directive dedup as the loop guard\",\"Letting a child inherit the full run-or-ask policy\"],\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\",\"AGENTS.md\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T09:55:20Z\",\"durationMs\":102000,\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q-failure-modes\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Which failure modes matter most for command surfacing\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-001\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Non-doctor command-versus-skill ties have no precedence rule\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-003\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Child sessions can start mutating commands without an ask\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-004\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Command workflows can re-enter routing on their own writes\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter010-001\",\"source\":\"f-iter010-001\",\"target\":\"q-failure-modes\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter010-002\",\"source\":\"f-iter010-003\",\"target\":\"q-failure-modes\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter010-003\",\"source\":\"f-iter010-004\",\"target\":\"q-failure-modes\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-001\",\"label\":\"Command-versus-skill ambiguity is by construction for non-doctor commands: /speckit:plan returns command-spec-kit 0.82/0.20 and system-spec-kit 0.82/0.18, inside the 0.05 ambiguity margins, and the brief has no precedence rule.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts:5\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md:17\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-002\",\"label\":\"Doctor bridges have a precedence rule non-doctor bridges lack: a typed doctor command puts its bridge first, passing doctor bridges sit after passing skills, and doctor bridges are removed before skill ambiguity is computed.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:914\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1225\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-003\",\"label\":\"A dispatched child session is the highest unsafe-run risk: AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 pre-resolves Gate 3 and turns stop-for-yes into record-and-continue, so a child with a run brief can start a mutating command with no user to answer.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\"AGENTS.md:84\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-004\",\"label\":\"The routing loop risk is partly controlled: Gate 2 fires before every code or Markdown write and command workflows write, while directive dedup suppresses repeated briefs but not repeated routing decisions.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\"AGENTS.md:68\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:40\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-005\",\"label\":\"The only anti-self-recommendation control is a -0.25 penalty against the advisor's own ids on audit or explainer prompts; it does not stop a command workflow from routing back into the advisor.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/scoring-constants.ts:237\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-006\",\"label\":\"Over-triggering is partly controlled by the -0.08 no-slash penalty and the read-only gate; the highest over-trigger surface is doctor lead_phrases, measured as disable comment hygiene gate leading with /doctor:git hooks.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1197\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:48\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-007\",\"label\":\"The brief budget tolerates one command line and one policy marker; a third consequence line competes with the fixed directive block and ambiguity head inside the 120-token cap, so the order should be command, policy, consequence.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:97\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md:25\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-008\",\"label\":\"Recommended controls: a same-owner command-versus-skill precedence rule, child authority limited to read-only or add-only commands, a route-once guard per turn and command, a diagnostic-only lead-phrase allowlist, and the command-policy-consequence line order.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:914\",\"AGENTS.md:84\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter010-009\",\"label\":\"Evidence against a blanket command-first rule: in the measured /speckit:plan case the skill has the lower uncertainty, so the rule must be scoped to a command and its own owner skill rather than applied to every command-skill pair.\",\"iteration\":10,\"sources\":[\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md:17\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"A blanket command-first tiebreak\",\"reason\":\"It would override a better-calibrated skill in the measured /speckit:plan case\",\"iteration\":10}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Relying on directive dedup as the loop guard\",\"reason\":\"It suppresses repeated briefs, not repeated routing decisions\",\"iteration\":10}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Letting a child inherit the full run-or-ask policy\",\"reason\":\"The child exemption removes the ask path, so mutating commands need a parent-authority rule\",\"iteration\":10}\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-010.jsonl"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-010.jsonl","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-010.jsonl","time":{"start":1794477334176,"end":1794477334186}},"id":"prt_1cf2f054900100ZSLQImQ4xf6U","sessionID":"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701","messageID":"msg_1cf2ef4de001UXxxAg5sT010HZ"}}
